  {"a":"yorick","b":"aatrox","win":["Aatrox","Aatrox","Skill","Skill","Skill","Yorick","Yorick"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 3-5","text":"Aatrox owns levels 1-2 because his Q1 Deathbringer Stance out-ranges and out-trades your point-blank Last Rites, and his passive-empowered auto heals through your poke. Once you hit 3 and can E-Mourning-Mist him then Q the slowed target, your all-in trade math evens out and it becomes a skill lane."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Both ults swing it, so 6 stays even: Maiden pressures, but World Ender (120s at rank 1) amplifies his healing and speed to win the long fight. Executioner's Calling cuts that engine — with Grievous Wounds on, his ult brawl stops out-sustaining you."},{"when":"1st item","text":"You favour the first-item window: Divine Sunderer/Shojin plus a full Cage lets you W-trap his dashes and grind him down with Maiden waves faster than he can Q-heal back. Aatrox's early trading edge fades as your souls stack."},{"when":"Late","text":"Yorick dominates 2+ items — you shove waves with Maiden, split-push towers, and your ghouls plus W-cage negate his combo in side-lane 1v1s. Aatrox needs teamfights; you take the map from him."}],"wants":{"you":["Reach lvl 3 to start E-into-Q trades","Full W Cage to trap his Q dashes and all-in","2+ items to split and 1v1 with Maiden"],"foe":["Level 1-2 auto-trades with empowered Q","Land all three Q sweetspots in a fight","World Ender resets to win extended brawls"]},"early":"Aatrox out-trades you at levels 1-2 — The Darkin Blade's outer edge out-ranges Last Rites and Deathbringer Stance heals the exchange back. His Q is 14s at rank 1: step in only after the third swing whiffs.","mid":"From level 3 it's a skill matchup: lead with Mourning Mist (E, 12s) to slow and shred his armor, then Last Rites the marked target while your ghouls sprint at it. Respect World Ender at 6 — commit only with Maiden up and Grievous Wounds already on him.","late":"Once your first item and rank-5 Dark Procession (12s) land you flip ahead: the wall blocks Umbral Dash out, Maiden grinds him down, and by 2+ items you out-split and out-1v1 him across the map.","whys":["Aatrox wins level 1 — his empowered auto and Q1 range beat your point-blank Last Rites trade.","Aatrox stays ahead at level 2 with a second Q and passive healing out-sustaining your poke.","Level 3 evens out once your E-slow into Q trade pattern comes online.","Levels 4-5 stay even as both champs trade with cooldowns and CS is contested.","Level 6 is a skill wash — Maiden versus World Ender both swing extended fights.","You favour the first-item spike: Cage plus bruiser item grinds through his Q sustain.","Yorick dominates 2+ items by out-splitting and 1v1ing with Maiden and ghouls."]},
  {"a":"yorick","b":"akali","win":["Yorick","Akali","Skill","Akali","Skill","Akali","Akali"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 3-5","text":"You win level 1 — Five Point Strike is her only damage and costs 110 energy at rank 1, so a Mourning Mist into Last Rites trade punishes her hard. Once Twilight Shroud is up at 2-3 she farms safely and Assassin's Mark autos win exchanges back; unselectable inside it, she makes your ghouls drop her."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Akali pulls ahead at 6 — Perfect Execution (120s at rank 1) gives two dashes to burst you and leave your Maiden behind, and its recast executes below a health threshold. Stay above that number and hold Dark Procession for her exit."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Akali favours the first-item window: Hextech Rocketbelt or Gunblade lets her one-combo squishies and burst you through your sustain before ghouls matter. Build early MR and don't over-extend without W up."},{"when":"Late","text":"Late game tilts on execution but the lock leans Akali — she roams and assassinates while you split. Your answer is to out-macro: shove with Maiden, take towers when she leaves, and never fight her without Cage to trap her Shroud escape."}],"wants":{"you":["Punish her weak level 1 with a mist-Q trade","W Cage to trap her Shroud or block R recast","Split and take towers when she roams mid"],"foe":["W Twilight Shroud to farm and drop your vision","Level 6 Perfect Execution double-dash burst","First assassin item to one-combo you"]},"early":"You own level 1 — Akali only has Q Five Point Strike, burns mana fast, and can't sustain, so land an E-mist Q trade and deny her early. Once her W Twilight Shroud is up she farms safely and her passive-empowered autos start winning the exchanges back.","mid":"Through mid it swings to Akali: inside Twilight Shroud (20s) she cannot be selected, so your ghouls and Maiden drop her, and at 6 Perfect Execution's dashes leave them behind. Hold Dark Procession for her exit, not her entry.","late":"With her first assassin item online she one-combos and roams; the matchup leans her way, so win it on the map — shove waves with Maiden, split for towers when she leaves, and only fight her with Cage ready.","whys":["You win level 1 — Akali has only Q for damage and no sustain, so you punish freely.","Akali takes level 2 once Twilight Shroud lets her farm safe and dodge your trades.","Level 3 is even as you get your full combo but she gets her Shroud spacing.","Akali favours levels 4-5, snowballing Q spam and shroud zoning into CS leads.","Level 6 is a skill window but her Perfect Execution burst is dangerous.","Akali favours the first-item spike — her assassin mythic one-combos through your sustain.","Akali stays ahead at 2+ items with roam pressure and pick potential."]},
  {"a":"yorick","b":"akshan","win":["Akshan","Akshan","Skill","Skill","Akshan","Skill","Yorick"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 3-5","text":"Akshan owns the early levels — his Q Avengerang and passive Dirty Fighting shield let him poke you from range and dodge your Last Rites while farming safely. From level 3 you can stabilise: use ghouls as a wave buffer and E Mourning Mist to slow him when he steps up, turning it into an even farming lane."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Akshan spikes at 6 — Comeuppance is long-range missing-health damage and Going Rogue camouflage lets him roam and resurrect off picks. Ping mid, sweep for him, and place Dark Procession across his path, never as a wall he can hook and swing off."},{"when":"1st item","text":"The first-item window is even: your ghoul stack plus Cage lets you all-in him if he mispositions, while his lethality item boosts his poke and roam. Trade only when his Q is down and E is on cooldown."},{"when":"Late","text":"Yorick pulls ahead 2+ items — you out-sidelane a squishy marksman and Maiden shoves faster than he can answer. Never wall his exit: Heroic Swing hooks terrain, so Dark Procession behind him is his anchor out, not your cage."}],"wants":{"you":["Reach lvl 3 to stabilise with ghoul wave buffer","Cage across his path — E hooks terrain behind him","2+ items to out-1v1 and split a squishy marksman"],"foe":["Q Avengerang poke behind Dirty Fighting shield","Level 6 Comeuppance execute and W roam","Lethality item to snowball poke and picks"]},"early":"Akshan controls levels 1-2 — his Q Avengerang out-ranges your point-blank Last Rites and his passive shield eats your poke while he farms from safety. Soak XP with ghouls, don't chase his Q, and wait for level 3 to steady the lane.","mid":"Levels 3-5 even out as your ghoul buffer and Mourning Mist's slow and armour shred let you contest CS, but he spikes at 6: Comeuppance hits from range and Going Rogue camouflages his roams. Buy a Control Ward — you have no reveal.","late":"By 2+ items you flip the lane — a squishy Akshan can't survive your ghouls and Cage in a sidelane 1v1, so split with Maiden, deny his roams by matching his shoves, and take towers to close it out.","whys":["Akshan wins level 1 — his Q out-ranges you and Dirty Fighting shield tanks your trade.","Akshan holds level 2 with continued ranged Q poke while you can't retaliate.","Level 3 evens as your ghoul buffer and E slow let you contest farm.","Levels 4-5 stay even with both trading cooldowns and holding CS.","Akshan spikes at 6 — Comeuppance execute plus W roam pressure swings tempo.","First-item window is even — your Cage all-in answers his lethality poke.","Yorick wins 2+ items by out-1v1ing and out-splitting the squishy marksman."]},
  {"a":"yorick","b":"ambessa","win":["Ambessa","Ambessa","Skill","Ambessa","Ambessa","Ambessa","Ambessa"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 3-5","text":"Ambessa dominates early — Cunning Sweep out-ranges you and Repudiation shields her, dealing MORE if it blocks your Last Rites, while Drakehound's Step sticks her to you through ghouls. Level 3 is the one even beat: bait Lacerate (13s), then Mourning Mist and Q the slow."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Ambessa spikes hard at 6 — Public Execution (130s) blinks 1250 units to the FARTHEST champion in its line, suppresses, then slams and stuns. You cannot act through it, so stand where a teammate, not you, is that farthest target."},{"when":"1st item","text":"First-item favours Ambessa: her bruiser mythic makes her chain-CC combo lethal and she out-trades you in the extended fights her kit is built for. Farm safe, build early armour, and let ghouls tank her poke."},{"when":"Late","text":"The lock leans Ambessa but late is your macro window — she's a teamfight diver, you're a split-pusher. Shove waves with Maiden, take side towers when she groups, and only 1v1 her with Cage ready to trap the dash chain."}],"wants":{"you":["Hit lvl 3 to bait dashes then E-mist Q","Cage her exit, not her R suppress","Split with Maiden while she looks to teamfight"],"foe":["Cunning Sweep range and a braced Repudiation","E dash chain to stick through ghouls","Level 6 Public Execution all-in burst"]},"early":"Ambessa runs the early lane — Cunning Sweep out-ranges your point-blank trade and Repudiation shields her, hitting harder if it blocks your damage, so give her nothing while she braces. Soak XP behind ghouls and give ground rather than feed a trade you'll lose.","mid":"Level 3 is your one even beat — bait Lacerate and Repudiation, then land Mourning Mist (12s) and Q the slowed target before her dashes reset. From 4 she reasserts control, and at 6 Public Execution suppresses you through anything you were holding.","late":"Ambessa favours the fights her kit wants, so beat her on the map instead: split-push with Maiden, punish her when she groups for teamfights, and only take a sidelane 1v1 with W Cage up to trap her dash chain.","whys":["Ambessa wins level 1 — Q range and W damage reduction beat your melee trade.","Ambessa holds level 2 with dash pressure and continued poke you can't answer.","Level 3 evens as you can bait her mobility then E-mist Q for a real trade.","Ambessa retakes levels 4-5 with her full combo and CS control.","Level 6 is a skill wash but her Public Execution all-in is the bigger threat.","Ambessa favours the first-item spike — her bruiser mythic wins extended fights.","Ambessa stays ahead at 2+ items as the superior teamfight diver."]},
  {"a":"yorick","b":"aurora","win":["Skill","Aurora","Aurora","Aurora","Aurora","Skill","Yorick"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 3-5","text":"Aurora controls the early lane — Twofold Hex (9s) pokes from range and Spirit Abjuration heals her off every spirit she exorcises, out-sustaining your chip. She keeps level 3 as well: The Weirding slows you and hops her back before your Mourning Mist matters."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Aurora spikes at 6 — Between Worlds (140s) leaves a slowing zone she can teleport across, and Across the Veil (22s) leaps her invisible out of your Maiden. Cage where she lands, and never fight inside the zone where its slow holds you."},{"when":"1st item","text":"First-item favours Aurora: a mage item bursts you through your sustain before ghouls stack, and The Weirding (15s) slows you into the rest of her combo. Build early MR and farm behind minions."},{"when":"Late","text":"Two items in, the side lane is yours — she wants teamfights and picks, you split-push. Shove with Maiden, take towers when she rotates, and duel her with Dark Procession ready to wall the Across the Veil escape."}],"wants":{"you":["Reach lvl 3 to block her Q with ghouls then E-mist","Cage her landing spot, not her E slow line","Split with Maiden while she seeks teamfights"],"foe":["Twofold Hex poke, Spirit Abjuration heals","The Weirding's slow into full combo","Level 6 Between Worlds zone and W reposition"]},"early":"Aurora runs the early lane — Twofold Hex out-ranges your melee trade and Spirit Abjuration heals her back off every spell she lands. Soak XP behind ghouls, block her Q with the wave, and bring Grievous Wounds early.","mid":"Levels 3-5 stay hers — use ghouls to eat her poke and only Mourning Mist (12s) her once The Weirding is spent. At 6 Between Worlds (140s) plus Across the Veil's invisible leap make her all-in and escape strong, so cage her landing spot.","late":"Once you have two items the side lane is yours: split-push with Maiden, punish her rotations by taking towers, and duel her with Dark Procession up to wall the Across the Veil escape.","whys":["Level 1 is even — her ranged Q pokes, but Last Rites heals the chip back.","Aurora holds level 2 with continued poke and her E stun threat.","Aurora holds 3 — The Weirding slows then hops her out of your reach.","Aurora retakes levels 4-5 with combo poke and CS control.","Level 6 is a skill wash but her Between Worlds all-in is the bigger threat.","Aurora favours the first-item spike — her mage mythic bursts through your sustain.","Yorick takes 2+ items — Maiden and ghouls out-duel her in the side lane."]},
  {"a":"yorick","b":"camille","win":["Camille","Camille","Skill","Camille","Skill","Camille","Camille"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 3-5","text":"Camille owns the early lane — her Q Precision Protocol true-damage second hit and W Tactical Sweep heal out-trade your Last Rites, and her passive Adaptive Defenses shield tanks your poke. Level 3 is even: bait her E hookshot into a wall, then E-mist and Q her while her mobility is on cooldown."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Camille spikes at 6 — The Hextech Ultimatum (140s) dashes to you and anchors you there for her full combo. Never wall her in: Dark Procession is terrain, and Hookshot pulls to walls, so your cage becomes her engage."},{"when":"1st item","text":"First-item strongly favours Camille: Divine Sunderer or Trinity makes her Q shred and her sustain outlasts your ghouls in extended trades. Build early armour, farm behind minions, and don't contest melee range."},{"when":"Late","text":"The lock stays Camille but late is your split window — she's a dive assassin, you're a wave-eating split-pusher. Shove with Maiden, take side towers, and fight her in open lane where she has no wall left to Hookshot off."}],"wants":{"you":["Hit lvl 3 to bait her E then E-mist Q","Cage her exit — a wall feeds her Hookshot","Split with Maiden while she looks to dive"],"foe":["Q true-damage and W heal to win early trades","Hookshot off any wall to engage or escape","Level 6 Hextech Ultimatum lockdown all-in"]},"early":"Camille runs levels 1-2 — Precision Protocol's delayed second hit lands as true damage and Tactical Sweep's outer half heals her, while Adaptive Defenses shields against your damage type. Buy Grievous Wounds early and fight away from walls.","mid":"Level 3 is your even beat — bait Hookshot (16s), then land Mourning Mist and Q while she has no mobility. She reasserts from 4, and at 6 The Hextech Ultimatum anchors you for a full combo, so cage her exit, never her approach.","late":"Camille favours the dive-and-pick game, so beat her on the map: split-push with Maiden, take towers when she rotates, and duel her away from terrain in the side lane — every wall is a Hookshot anchor for her.","whys":["Camille wins level 1 — Q true damage and W heal beat your point-blank trade.","Camille holds level 2 with shield uptime and continued trade dominance.","Level 3 evens as you can bait her E then E-mist Q with her mobility down.","Camille retakes levels 4-5 with combo damage and CS control.","Level 6 is a skill wash but her Ultimatum lockdown all-in is the bigger threat.","Camille favours the first-item spike — Sunderer sustain outlasts your ghouls.","Camille stays ahead at 2+ items as the superior dive-and-pick threat."]},
  {"a":"yorick","b":"cassiopeia","win":["Cassiopeia","Cassiopeia","Skill","Cassiopeia","Skill","Cassiopeia","Cassiopeia"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 3-5","text":"Cassiopeia controls the early lane — Noxious Blast (3.5s) and Twin Fang spam grind you from range while Miasma (24s) slows you and cuts your ghouls off from her. Level 3 is even: soak Q with ghouls and Mourning Mist her when she steps into your minions to farm."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Cassiopeia spikes at 6 — Petrifying Gaze (120s) stuns everyone facing her and only slows those turned away, so turn as it lands. Commit after Miasma is spent, and hold Dark Procession for her retreat, not her approach."},{"when":"1st item","text":"First-item favours Cassiopeia hard: her E scales to a machine-gun and her mana sustain lets her poke endlessly, out-DPSing your ghoul stack before you close range. Build early MR and Merc treads, farm behind minions."},{"when":"Late","text":"The lock stays Cassiopeia but late is your split window — she's an immobile teamfight mage grounded by her own kit. Shove with Maiden, take side towers away from her, and never facecheck her R; force her to defend towers where your ghouls swarm her."}],"wants":{"you":["Hit lvl 3 to soak Q with ghouls then E-mist","W Cage and side approach vs her R stun","Split with Maiden away from her teamfight range"],"foe":["Q and E poke to grind you from range","Miasma to slow you and cut off your ghouls","Level 6 Petrifying Gaze stun to deny all-ins"]},"early":"Cassiopeia runs levels 1-2 — Noxious Blast and Twin Fang out-poke your melee kit, and Twin Fang heals her off every tick of it. Soak XP behind ghouls, buy Grievous Wounds early, and keep the wave between you and her Miasma.","mid":"Level 3 is your even beat — let ghouls eat her poke, then E Mourning Mist and Q when she comes to CS. She reasserts from 4, and at 6 Petrifying Gaze stuns any frontal approach, so come from the side and hold Cage for her commit.","late":"Cassiopeia favours the poke-and-teamfight game, so beat her on the map: split-push with Maiden away from her range, take towers, and force her to defend where your ghouls swarm her — never facecheck her R.","whys":["Cassiopeia wins level 1 — Q and E poke plus Miasma ground beat your melee approach.","Cassiopeia holds level 2 with continued ranged DPS you can't retaliate against.","Level 3 evens as ghouls soak her poke and you can E-mist a trade.","Cassiopeia retakes levels 4-5 with escalating E spam and CS control.","Level 6 is a skill wash but her Petrifying Gaze stun denies your all-ins.","Cassiopeia favours the first-item spike — her E out-DPSes your ghoul stack.","Cassiopeia stays ahead at 2+ items with unrelenting poke and teamfight range."]},
  {"a":"yorick","b":"chogath","win":["Skill","Skill","Skill","Yorick","Yorick","Yorick","Cho'Gath"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 3-5","text":"Once your W wall is up you can cage Cho and free-hit him while E slows him for guaranteed Q procs; his only trade tool is a slow, telegraphed Q rupture you sidestep on the E-slow."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Your R ghouls plus Maiden shove waves he can't match, and his level-6 Feast is a single-target execute that does nothing to your ghoul army — you dictate the map."},{"when":"1st item","text":"After Tiamat/Divine Sunderer your ghoul stacks and Maiden turn every all-in in your favour; Cho has to burn Feast on Maiden or lose the tower."},{"when":"Late","text":"Late Cho stacks Feast HP and tankiness, and once he has Feast stacks plus Zhonya's he can body-block your split and one-shot the Maiden, flipping the sidelane."}],"wants":{"you":["W caging him for free Q/E procs","Ghoul + Maiden wave pressure to shove and roam","Snowballing a lead before Cho out-scales you"],"foe":["Landing Q rupture into Feast to burst you","Stacking Feast HP to become unkillable","Reaching 6 items where his tankiness ignores your ghouls"]},"early":"Levels 1-2 are even farm — Cho pokes with Rupture (6s, 950 range) and Vorpal Spikes on the wave, and Carnivore heals him off every minion he kills, so chip alone will never stick. Neither of you threatens a kill this early; last-hit with Last Rites, stay outside Feral Scream's 300-range cone, and save Mourning Mist for the level-3 commit.","mid":"From level 3 your W Dark Procession changes the lane: wall him in, E Mourning Mist for the slow and vision, and auto-Q him while he can't reach you. Through 6 your ghouls and Maiden of the Mist out-shove his wave so you take plates and pressure his tower. This is your window — every trade under your wall and every ghoul on the wave stacks a lead before Cho's scaling comes online.","late":"Once Cho has Feast stacks and a first big item his effective HP balloons and your ghoul chunks stop mattering; his Feast becomes a true-damage execute that deletes your Maiden and threatens you in any extended fight. Play the 2+ item phase as a split-pusher — use ghouls and Maiden to siege a sidelane and force him to answer, never a straight 1v1 into a stacked Cho with Zhonya's.","whys":["Level 1 is a neutral farm lane where neither Yorick nor Cho'Gath can threaten a kill.","Level 2 stays even as Cho's Q poke trades against your minion soak.","Level 3 is even until your W is reliably up to cage him.","Levels 4-5 favour Yorick because W-cage plus E-slow lets you free-hit him for guaranteed Q procs.","Level 6 favours Yorick as R ghouls and Maiden out-shove Cho's wave while Feast does nothing to your army.","First item favours Yorick — Tiamat/Sunderer plus Maiden win every all-in before Cho scales.","Two-plus items flip to Cho'Gath, whose stacked Feast HP and true-damage execute ignore your ghoul chip."]},
  {"a":"yorick","b":"darius","win":["Darius","Darius","Darius","Skill","Yorick","Yorick","Yorick"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 3-5","text":"With W up you cage Darius outside his Q outer-ring healing range and E-slow him so he can never land the outer-Q; freed from his heal, you win the sustained trade."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Level 6 tips to you — Noxian Guillotine (120s) hits harder per Hemorrhage stack, but Maiden and ghouls force his pull-Q-W combo to chew through bodies first, so the dunk lands late."},{"when":"1st item","text":"After Divine Sunderer your ghoul-backed all-ins out-DPS his bleed; if he pulls you into the wall you cage HIM and turn the flip."},{"when":"Late","text":"Your Maiden and ghoul army let you split and 1v1 or 1v2 sidelane, and a fed Yorick out-duels Darius through the wall while he needs 5-stack bleed to threaten you."}],"wants":{"you":["W to cage him away from outer-Q heal","Grievous Wounds to kill the Decimate heal","Ghoul + Maiden bodies to eat his Q and R"],"foe":["Landing outer-ring Q for heal and max trade","Apprehend E pulling you into his combo","Stacking Hemorrhage to 5 for a Guillotine reset"]},"early":"Levels 1-2 belong to Darius — he walks up to land the blade edge of Decimate (9s) for the heal and the big damage, so sit behind the minions and last-hit with Last Rites. Apprehend is 26s at rank 1: once he spends it you have half a minute of safety. Buy Grievous Wounds early, because that Decimate heal is what wins him every long trade.","mid":"From 4 the lane tilts to you: drop Dark Procession (20s) to cage Darius, Mourning Mist for the slow and armour shred, and stand where only the handle of Decimate can reach you. Level 6 is yours — Guillotine still executes, but ghouls and Maiden are bodies his pull-Q combo has to chew through first, so fight with the army up. Every caged trade where he misses the blade is free damage toward your first item.","late":"With Divine Sunderer and a ghoul lead your all-ins out-damage his bleed, and if he Apprehends you into your own wall you simply cage him and win the flip. Two-plus items you become the premier split-pusher: Maiden and ghouls let you siege and 1v1 a sidelane, and a fed Yorick beats Darius straight up while he needs a full 5-stack bleed to even threaten the Guillotine reset.","whys":["Darius owns level 1 — his blade-edge Decimate out-damages anything you have yet.","Darius keeps level 2 — Crippling Strike slows you into his blade edge.","Darius holds 3 until Dark Procession is up to cage him.","Levels 4-5 favour Yorick because W-cage plus E-slow denies his healing outer-Q.","Level 6 goes to you — Maiden and ghouls outlast his Guillotine dunk and out-damage it.","First item favours Yorick as Sunderer-backed ghoul all-ins out-DPS his bleed.","Two-plus items favour Yorick, whose Maiden split and duel power beat a bleed-reliant Darius."]},
  {"a":"yorick","b":"drmundo","win":["Skill","Yorick","Yorick","Yorick","Skill","Yorick","Yorick"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 3-5","text":"Mourning Mist marks Mundo, shreds his armour and sprints your ghouls at him; Dark Procession cages the retreat, though it is destructible and he will swing at it. Bring Grievous Wounds — his regen beats raw chip."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Mundo's R gives him big HP and regen, but your R Maiden and ghouls out-DPS the heal and keep shoving; he ults to survive, not to kill you."},{"when":"1st item","text":"After Divine Sunderer your %HP on-hit and ghoul stacks tear through Mundo's stacked health, and Maiden lets you dive his tower faster than he heals."},{"when":"Late","text":"Yorick's ghoul army and Maiden apply constant %-HP and let you split-push through Mundo, who can tank but can't kill you or match your wave pressure."}],"wants":{"you":["Wall his retreat, not his Q","E-slow for free Q procs and ghoul hits","Maiden + ghoul %HP pressure to out-shove and dive"],"foe":["Landing Q Infected Bonesaw to poke and slow","Stacking HP/regen to survive and out-farm","Heart Zapper storing your damage as a heal"]},"early":"Level 1 is even farm — Infected Bonesaw (4s) chunks you off your current health and slows, so sidestep it and last-hit with Last Rites. Goes Where He Pleases resists the first immobilise that hits him, and his regen refills whatever you poke off, so don't start an HP war. Soak XP and set up your level-2/3 spike.","mid":"From level 2-3 you own the lane: W Dark Procession walls off his cleaver line, E Mourning Mist slows him for guaranteed Q hits, and your ghouls chew his HP faster than his regen restores it. Through 6 keep shoving with ghouls and Maiden — Mundo's ult is a survival tool that heals him, not a kill threat, so you out-shove and take plates or dive. This whole stretch is yours; press the tempo and deny him comfortable farm.","late":"With Divine Sunderer your %-max-HP on-hit plus stacking ghouls melt even a full-HP Mundo, and Maiden lets you tower-dive faster than he heals. Two-plus items you become the split-push nightmare: constant ghoul %-HP damage and Maiden pressure mean Mundo can soak your poke but never kill you or match your wave clear, so you take the map while he farms.","whys":["Level 1 is even — Mundo's cleaver poke is offset by his regen making early trades moot.","Level 2 favours Yorick as your W and ghouls begin out-pressuring his health bar.","Level 3 favours Yorick because W-cage plus E-slow gives free Q procs he can't answer.","Levels 4-5 favour Yorick as ghoul %HP chip beats Mundo's passive regen in lane.","Level 6 is even — his R heal buys survival but doesn't threaten a kill on you.","First item favours Yorick as Sunderer %HP and Maiden out-damage his stacked HP.","Two-plus items favour Yorick, whose ghoul army and split pressure Mundo can't match."]},
  {"a":"yorick","b":"fiora","win":["Fiora","Fiora","Skill","Fiora","Skill","Fiora","Fiora"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 3-5","text":"Riposte (24s at rank 1) parries your damage and any Maiden auto, and Lunge (13s) dances her around your wall onto Duelist's Dance Vitals; you cannot pin a champion who dashes and parries on demand."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Grand Challenge (110s) reveals four Vitals for true damage and heals her through your ghouls, so refuse the all-in until Grievous Wounds is on her."},{"when":"1st item","text":"After first item Fiora's tankbuster kit and Riposte cooldown make her out-duel you in any bracket; parrying your E turns your engage into her burst window."},{"when":"Late","text":"Late Fiora with Riposte up 1v1s Yorick through Maiden — her true damage and vital heals shrug off ghoul chip, and she splits as well as you do."}],"wants":{"you":["W wall to block her Lunge escape angle","E-slow only when her Riposte is down","Ghoul + Maiden bodies to soak vital procs"],"foe":["Riposte parrying your damage window","Q Lunge dancing around vitals and your wall","R Grand Challenge true damage + heal to out-duel"]},"early":"Levels 1-2 belong to Fiora — she walks up, Lunges to your revealed Vital, and her early Q damage plus the Vital heal out-trade your autos. Riposte stuns only if it blocks an immobilise and nothing in your kit immobilises, so it eats your damage but never locks you down. Farm defensively with Last Rites, give ground rather than feed Vitals, and buy Grievous Wounds early.","mid":"At 3-5 she snowballs with Riposte (24s at rank 1), which parries your damage and any Maiden auto outright, and Lunge weaves her around Dark Procession onto Vitals. Commit only once Riposte is spent, and wall her escape lane rather than trying to trap her. Grand Challenge (110s) is an all-in you refuse without ghouls, Maiden and Grievous Wounds — its true damage and heal out-sustain raw chip every time.","late":"First item and beyond, Fiora out-duels you in nearly every bracket: Riposte's low cooldown neuters your engage tools and her vital true-damage heals through ghoul pressure. Don't 1v1 her in the sidelane — instead use ghouls and Maiden to push a different lane and take map objectives with your team, converting your wave pressure into cross-map value rather than a losing duel.","whys":["Level 1 favours Fiora — her Q Lunge and early vital trades beat your autos.","Level 2 favours Fiora as her poke and vital procs out-trade you.","Level 3 is even until your W and Maiden are online to contest.","Levels 4-5 favour Fiora because Riposte parries your E and Q Lunge dodges your wall.","Level 6 is even — her Grand Challenge all-in is offset by your Maiden and ghoul bodies.","First item favours Fiora, whose Riposte cooldown and vitals out-duel you.","Two-plus items favour Fiora, who 1v1s through Maiden and splits as well as you."]},
  {"a":"yorick","b":"galio","win":["Yorick","Skill","Skill","Yorick","Yorick","Yorick","Yorick"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 3-5","text":"W caging Galio plus E-slow lets you free-hit him while he can't reliably land the second hit of his Q Winds of War; your ghouls out-DPS his magic-shield sustain in melee range."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Galio's R is a roam/peel tool, not a lane-kill button — while he's tempted to ult bot, your ghouls and Maiden shove and take his tower."},{"when":"1st item","text":"After Divine Sunderer your ghoul-backed all-ins beat his tanky mage stats, and if he E-taunt-dashes in you cage him with W and win the flip."},{"when":"Late","text":"Yorick's Maiden and ghoul army let you split and siege, and Galio — built to peel and roam — can't 1v1 your army in the sidelane."}],"wants":{"you":["W to cage him and cut his Q line","E-slow for free Q procs and ghoul hits","Ghoul + Maiden pressure to shove and deny roams"],"foe":["Landing both hits of Q for poke and heal","Justice Punch into a Durand taunt","R roam to snowball other lanes instead"]},"early":"Level 1 is yours — Galio is a weak early laner who wants to poke with Q Winds of War and stall to scale, and you can walk up behind minions, E Mourning Mist, and Q him before his shield sustain matters. Deny him free Q pokes and keep the wave moving so he can't farm comfortably. His combo opens with the Colossal Smash reset, so the auto wind-up is your cue to step back, not the cast.","mid":"From 3 you cage him with W Dark Procession, E-slow him, and free-hit him where he can't land the back half of his Q. Levels 4-6 you out-shove with ghouls and Maiden and threaten his tower; his R is a roam/peel tool, so when he's tempted to ult another lane you punish the wave and take plates. Watch his E taunt-dash — bait it, then cage him and win the return trade. This whole stretch is a shove-and-pressure clinic in your favour.","late":"With Divine Sunderer and a ghoul lead your all-ins beat his tanky-mage stat line, and any E engage just feeds your W cage. Two-plus items you're the better split-pusher by a mile: Maiden and ghouls let you siege a sidelane and 1v1 or 1v2, while Galio — designed to peel and teamfight-roam — has no answer to your army alone.","whys":["Level 1 favours Yorick against a weak-early Galio you out-trade behind minions.","Level 2 is even as Galio pokes Q while you soak and set up.","Level 3 is even until your W-cage is reliably online.","Levels 4-5 favour Yorick because W-cage plus E-slow gives free Q procs.","Level 6 favours Yorick as ghouls and Maiden out-shove while his R only roams.","First item favours Yorick, whose Sunderer ghoul all-ins beat his tank-mage stats.","Two-plus items favour Yorick, whose Maiden split army Galio can't 1v1."]},
  {"a":"yorick","b":"gangplank","win":["Yorick","Yorick","Skill","Skill","Yorick","Yorick","Gangplank"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 3-5","text":"Early you walk him down — W caging GP plus E-slow lets you free-hit him, and pre-barrel-mastery his Q Parrrley poke can't out-damage your ghoul-backed all-in."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Your R Maiden and ghouls shove hard and let you all-in before his barrel chains come online; deny his citrus-heal by forcing fights, not poke wars."},{"when":"1st item","text":"With Tiamat/Sunderer up you can still burst him through his barrels if you cage the detonation and dodge the chain — punish his early item timings."},{"when":"Late","text":"Once GP has Trinity + Sheen crits and full barrel mastery his Q one-shots minions and pokes you out, and Cannon Barrage's true damage ignores any armour or MR you stack against him."}],"wants":{"you":["W to cage him off his barrel chains","E-slow to deny barrel spacing and land Q","Ghoul all-ins before his item spikes hit"],"foe":["Landing chained barrels for combo burst","Remove Scurvy to cleanse your E slow","Scaling crits and global R to take over"]},"early":"Levels 1-2 favour you — Gangplank is gold-starved early and relies on Q Parrrley for last-hits, so you walk up, E Mourning Mist, and out-trade him with autos and ghouls before his barrels chain. Punish every Q he uses on a minion by stepping in. Don't let him free-farm into his item spikes; the earlier you make this lane miserable, the better, because time is entirely on his side.","mid":"At 3-6 keep the pressure on: W Dark Procession caging him off his barrel chains, E-slow to break his barrel spacing, and all-in with ghouls and Maiden rather than trading poke. Remove Scurvy cures that slow and heals him on a 22s cooldown at rank 1 — bait it, commit inside those 22 seconds, and carry Grievous Wounds into every extended trade. Force fights while your ghoul all-in still out-damages his combo.","late":"This is his phase — with Trinity Force, Sheen crits, and full barrel mastery his Q one-shots minions and chips you from screens away, and his global R plus barrel zones out-teamfight and out-scale your split. Once he has items, stop dueling him: use ghouls and Maiden to push a sidelane and take objectives with your team before his crit-barrel scaling turns the game. Your only win condition late is tempo and map play, not a 1v1.","whys":["Level 1 favours Yorick against a gold-starved GP you out-trade with autos and ghouls.","Level 2 favours Yorick as W and E let you punish his Parrrley last-hits.","Level 3 is even as his barrels begin to matter and your all-in is still strong.","Levels 4-5 are even — trades balance between his barrels and your ghoul pressure.","Level 6 favours Yorick as Maiden and ghouls let you all-in before barrel chains scale.","First item favours Yorick, who can still burst him through barrels with a cage.","Two-plus items favour Gangplank, whose crit barrels and global R out-scale your split."]},
  {"a":"yorick","b":"garen","win":["Garen","Garen","Garen","Yorick","Yorick","Yorick","Yorick"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 3-5","text":"W caging Garen plus E-slow lets you free-hit him — but Decisive Strike breaks every slow on cast, so wall the ground he must walk rather than his feet; ghouls out-chew his regen and W tenacity."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Garen's R Demacian Justice executes low targets, but your R Maiden and ghouls keep you topped and shoving; his ult is a pick tool, not a way to win the shove."},{"when":"1st item","text":"After Divine Sunderer your %HP ghoul all-ins beat his Stridebreaker bruiser stats, and he has no dash — a cage behind him is a walk he cannot make."},{"when":"Late","text":"Yorick's Maiden and ghoul army out-split Garen — he can 1v1 a squishy but can't kill you through Maiden or match your wave clear and siege."}],"wants":{"you":["W across the ground he must walk","E-slow for free Q procs and ghoul hits","Ghoul + Maiden pressure to out-shove and split"],"foe":["Q Decisive Strike silence to cancel your combo","Spinning E while W tanks your ghoul chip","R execute to snag a pick when you're low"]},"early":"Levels 1-2 are his — Garen walks up, Q Decisive Strike to silence and burst, then spins E and backs off behind his passive regen. Decisive Strike is an auto-attack reset, so the wind-up is your cue to step back, not the cast. Farm with Last Rites, respect the 300-range Q, and hold your E charge until W is online rather than proving a point.","mid":"At 3 the lane opens for you: W Dark Procession caging Garen, E Mourning Mist for the slow, and free autos while he walks — there is no dash in his kit. Decisive Strike purges that slow and silences you on a flat 8s cooldown, so open the moment it is spent. Your ghouls chew through him faster than his W tenacity and regen can heal. Demacian Justice is true damage and an execute — stay topped with Maiden and it never triggers.","late":"With Divine Sunderer your %-HP ghoul all-ins beat his Stridebreaker bruiser build, and with no dash in his kit a cage between you is a walk he cannot make. Two-plus items you're the superior split-pusher: Maiden and ghouls let you siege and 1v1 or 1v2 a sidelane, while Garen can delete a squishy but can't kill you through Maiden or match your map pressure.","whys":["Level 1 is Garen's — his 300-range Q silence beats your empty kit.","Level 2 is Garen's as his Q-E poke beats a minion soak with no ghouls.","Level 3 is Garen's until your W-cage is reliably online.","Levels 4-5 favour Yorick because W-cage plus E-slow gives free Q procs he can't answer.","Level 6 favours Yorick — Maiden keeps you over his R execute threshold.","First item favours Yorick as Sunderer %HP ghoul all-ins beat his bruiser stats.","Two-plus items favour Yorick, whose Maiden split army out-duels and out-sieges Garen."]},
  {"a":"yorick","b":"gnar","win":["Gnar","Gnar","Gnar","Gnar","Skill","Gnar","Yorick"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 3-5","text":"Once your W wall is up you get a window: fight around your ghouls when Gnar's Boomerang Throw (Q) is down, since he loses most of his poke and can't kite the wall."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Gnar's danger spike is Mega form, not your R — bait him to burn Rage before he transforms, then all-in Mini Gnar with E-slow, ghouls, and your Maiden while he can't GNAR! wall you."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Gnar's first item plus his Rage-timed jumps let him poke your ghouls apart with Hyper (W) procs and boomerang from range, tilting spacing back to him."},{"when":"Late","text":"Split-push relentlessly — Gnar has no hard wave clear and struggles to duel your full ghoul-and-Maiden squad in a side lane, so make him choose between defending and grouping."}],"wants":{"you":["Fight when his Boomerang (Q) and Hop (E) are both down","Push and crash waves so his poke can't reset for free","Force the all-in on Mini Gnar, never Mega"],"foe":["Poke your ghouls and health with Q boomerang + W Hyper procs","Bank Rage to hit Mega and GNAR! (R) you into wall or minions","Kite the lane at range and deny your ghoul stacks"]},"early":"Gnar owns levels 1-2: his Boomerang Throw (Q) out-ranges your Last Rites and his Hyper passive shreds you before your ghouls stack, so eat the poke and just farm with Q resets.","mid":"The tide turns at 4-5 — your Dark Procession wall traps Mini Gnar, and with ghouls plus E-slow you win the short trade whenever his Q is on cooldown; keep him in Mini and punish the Rage gaps.","late":"Once Gnar itemizes and his Rage timing is reliable he pokes your ghoul waves apart and swings Mega fights, so stop trying to teamfight him and split-push where his lack of clear and single-target kit can't answer your Maiden.","whys":["Gnar's Boomerang Throw out-ranges Last Rites at level 1, so he pokes you freely before ghouls come online.","At level 2 his Hyper procs and Q poke keep chunking you while you still lack the wall to fight back.","By level 3 your W wall and first ghouls even the trades, making it a skill window.","At levels 4-5 Hop leaps your wall and Boomerang Throw returns every 16s, so he still sets the spacing.","Level 6 is roughly even — your R answers his Mega threat but only if you dodge the GNAR! timing.","With first item and reliable Rage, Gnar out-pokes your ghoul spacing and swings Mega, favouring him.","In the 2+ item stage your Maiden-and-ghoul split beats a Gnar with no wave clear, so make him answer the side lane."]},
  {"a":"yorick","b":"gragas","win":["Gragas","Skill","Skill","Gragas","Yorick","Yorick","Yorick"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 3-5","text":"Respect Barrel Roll early — 10s at rank 1 — and the moment he spends Body Slam to trade, cage him: it is 14s down, and Dark Procession is terrain his charge cannot cross anyway."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Your ult flips the lane: summon Maiden into a trade and Gragas can't out-sustain the combined ghoul-and-Maiden DPS, and his Explosive Cask (R) knockback can't peel a full ghoul wave."},{"when":"1st item","text":"After your first item Gragas becomes mostly a utility body — you out-duel him easily, so trade whenever his Q or E is on cooldown."},{"when":"Late","text":"Gragas offers nothing in a 1v1 side lane; shove and split, and if he rotates to stop you your Maiden plus ghouls win the duel outright."}],"wants":{"you":["Wall the lane he Body Slams through — terrain stops the dash","Trade with Maiden up when his Q barrel is down","Split-push — he can't 1v1 your ghoul squad"],"foe":["Poke you down with Barrel Roll (Q) at levels 1-4","Use Body Slam (E) into Cask (R) to disengage your ghouls","Roam and use his kit as teamfight utility rather than dueling"]},"early":"Gragas edges level 1 with his Barrel Roll (Q) range and passive sustain, out-poking your Last Rites before you have ghouls, so farm safely and don't walk into barrels.","mid":"Through levels 2-3 it's even as your ghouls come online, but he reclaims a slight edge at 4-5 when his Q is maxed and hits hard — wall him only when his Body Slam (E) is spent so he can't slide out.","late":"From level 6 onward you take over: Maiden plus ghouls out-sustain and out-DPS his kit, his Explosive Cask (R) can't peel the swarm, and after first item you win every even-cooldown trade and dominate the side lane.","whys":["Gragas out-ranges you at level 1 with Barrel Roll and his passive keeps him healthy through your poke.","By level 2-3 your ghouls arrive and match his poke, making it a skill lane.","Level 3 stays even as neither champ can commit a clean kill yet.","At levels 4-5 max-rank Barrel Roll poke and his Body Slam mobility tilt trades back to Gragas.","Level 6 flips to you — Maiden's DPS plus ghouls overwhelm his sustain and Cask can't clear the wall.","With first item your dueling outpaces his utility-focused kit, favouring Yorick.","In the 2+ item stage Gragas can't 1v1 your ghoul-and-Maiden squad, so you own the side lane."]},
  {"a":"yorick","b":"graves","win":["Graves","Graves","Graves","Skill","Graves","Graves","Yorick"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 3-5","text":"Graves shreds ghouls and health with End of the Line (Q) and his 4-bullet shotgun, so don't stack trades — use ghouls as chip and farm with Last Rites behind your wall."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Even with Maiden up, Quickdraw dashes him clear and refunds its own cooldown off every auto, so summon R only once he has committed and those 16s are genuinely running."},{"when":"1st item","text":"His first-item spike — End of the Line plus the True Grit resists Quickdraw stacks — wins extended fights, so keep pushing and pressuring rather than dueling head-on."},{"when":"Late","text":"By two-plus items your ghoul wall and Maiden finally out-grind his cooldown-reliant burst in a 1v1, so split-push and force him to commit Quickdraw before you all-in."}],"wants":{"you":["Farm safely with Q resets and avoid extended trades","Wall once Quickdraw's 16s is truly running","Scale to 2 items and split where his burst can't one-shot the swarm"],"foe":["Shred ghouls with End of the Line and shotgun autos","Dash out of the wall with Quickdraw (E) to reset trades","End fights fast before your Maiden out-grinds him"]},"early":"Graves dominates levels 1-3: End of the Line (Q) plus his shotgun autos out-trade you hard and clear ghouls faster than you stack them, so farm and never fight into a loaded gun.","mid":"It stays his through the mid-game — level 4-5 is a brief skill window where a good wall can punish a whiffed Q, but at 6 his Quickdraw (E) mobility lets him slip your Dark Procession and re-burst, keeping him ahead.","late":"You only take over at two-plus items, when your ghoul wall and Maiden's sustained DPS finally out-grind his burst; until then respect the shred, farm up, and win the game by split-pushing where his single-target kit can't stop your Maiden.","whys":["Graves out-trades level 1 with End of the Line and a 4-bullet shotgun passive before ghouls matter.","At level 2 his Q shred and autos keep chunking you faster than your ghouls stack.","By level 3 End of the Line is down to 9.5s and he still controls every trade.","Levels 4-5 are roughly even as your wall and ghoul count finally let you punish whiffs.","At level 6 his Quickdraw dash escapes your wall and re-bursts, tilting it back to Graves.","With first item his Q shred and armor stacks win extended fights over your ghouls.","In the 2+ item stage your ghoul-and-Maiden grind finally beats his burst, giving you the side lane."]},
  {"a":"yorick","b":"gwen","win":["Skill","Skill","Skill","Skill","Skill","Gwen","Gwen"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 3-5","text":"The early lane is an even farm race — trade with ghouls and E-slow when her Skip 'n Slash (E) is down, since without the dash she can't reposition out of your wall."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Even at 6 it's a skill fight: she is untargetable from outside Hallowed Mist, but anything inside can hit her — send the swarm in on a Mourning Mist mark instead of waiting out the 22s."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Gwen's first item is her real spike — Snip Snip! (Q) is true damage down its centre, so armour and MR both read the trade wrong, and Hallowed Mist shrugs off your squad."},{"when":"Late","text":"With items Gwen out-duels and out-splits you thanks to W immunity and Q shred; don't 1v1 her — group with your team where ghouls add DPS she can't W away from."}],"wants":{"you":["Trade when her Skip 'n Slash (E) dash is down","Bait or fight at the edge of Hallowed Mist (W)","Play with your team so ghouls add DPS she can't ignore"],"foe":["Sit in Hallowed Mist (W) to ignore ghouls and your Maiden","Shred ghouls and HP with Snip Snip! (Q)","Use Skip 'n Slash (E) to dodge your wall and reset the duel"]},"early":"It's a dead-even farm lane through level 5 — neither of you kills the other cleanly; trade with ghouls and E-slow only when her Skip 'n Slash (E) is unavailable so she can't dance out of your wall.","mid":"Level 6 stays a skill matchup. Hallowed Mist only protects her from enemies outside it — mark her with Mourning Mist and your Mist Walkers walk into the fog and keep swinging while you work its edge. It is 22s at rank 1.","late":"Once Gwen buys her first item she pulls ahead for good — Snip Snip! melts ghouls and health while Hallowed Mist and Skip 'n Slash dodge the swarm, and Needlework is her R, three casts of slowing needles. Stop dueling: group and let ghouls chip her from inside the fog.","whys":["Level 1 is an even farm start with neither champ threatening a kill.","At level 2 trades stay balanced as ghouls and Snip Snip! roughly cancel out.","By level 3 it's still skill-dependent, decided by dashes and wall timing.","Levels 4-5 remain even since her W and your wall trade off cleanly.","Level 6 is a skill fight — Maiden pressures her but Hallowed Mist negates ghouls.","With first item Snip Snip!'s true core plus Hallowed Mist win her the duel.","In the 2+ item stage Gwen out-duels and out-splits you, so she owns the side lane."]},
  {"a":"yorick","b":"heimerdinger","win":["Skill","Heimerdinger","Skill","Heimerdinger","Yorick","Heimerdinger","Yorick"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 3-5","text":"His H-28G Turrets (Q) zone you off the wave and chunk you with beam poke, so use ghouls to soak turret shots and only step up when he's placed turrets defensively and can't re-poke."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"This is your one window — summon Maiden and dive: your ghouls plus Maiden shred his turret nest faster than he can re-lay it, and he has no dash to escape your Dark Procession wall."},{"when":"1st item","text":"After first item Heimer's CDR lets him keep three turrets up permanently and his Grenade (E) stun peels your all-in, so he reclaims lane control."},{"when":"Late","text":"By two items you out-siege him: ghouls and Maiden grind his turrets down faster than he re-lays them, and Heimerdinger himself cannot duel you or leave a cage without a dash."}],"wants":{"you":["Use ghouls to eat turret shots before you commit","All-in at 6 with Maiden before his CDR spikes","Wall him during the dive so his Grenade (E) stun is his only out"],"foe":["Zone the wave with H-28G Turrets (Q) and beam poke","Stun your all-in with CH-2 Electron Storm Grenade","Keep permanent turret uptime after first item to wall you off"]},"early":"Level 1 is even with a single H-28 G turret down, but from 2 he owns the lane — turret beams plus 1325-range Hextech Micro-Rockets out-range everything you have, so give ground, soak shots with ghouls, and survive to 6.","mid":"Level 3 offers a brief skill window, but he's back ahead at 4-5 with a full turret nest; your real spike is level 6, where Maiden plus ghouls dive and delete his turrets faster than he can rebuild, and no dash saves him from your wall.","late":"Once Heimer hits his first item his CDR gives permanent triple-turret uptime and the 11s grenade stun peels your dive. By two items it flips back: ghouls and Maiden grind turrets down faster than he re-lays them, and he still has no dash out of Dark Procession, so take the side lane he cannot personally hold.","whys":["Level 1 is even — one turret out and no Micro-Rockets yet, so just farm the wave.","At level 2 his turret poke keeps chunking you before your ghouls come online.","Level 3 is a brief skill window as your ghouls let you contest the wave.","At levels 4-5 a full turret nest reclaims lane control for Heimer.","Level 6 is your spike — Maiden plus ghouls dive and shred his turrets with no escape for him.","With first item his CDR gives permanent turrets and his Grenade stun re-walls you off.","In the 2+ item stage Maiden and ghouls out-siege a Heimer who cannot duel."]},
  {"a":"yorick","b":"illaoi","win":["Skill","Skill","Skill","Skill","Yorick","Yorick","Yorick"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 3-5","text":"Never fight in her tentacle field — dodge Test of Spirit, 16s at rank 1 from 900 range — and remember Harsh Lesson is what drags the slams onto you, so its wind-up is the moment to step out, not the cast."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"You tip ahead here: your Maiden and ghouls tank tentacle slams and out-DPS her, and if she ults you can wall off the tentacles with Dark Procession so they can't all connect."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Your first-item spike lets ghouls plus Maiden out-sustain her Prophet-of-an-Elder-God healing, so you win extended trades as long as your Spirit isn't ripped out."},{"when":"Late","text":"You out-split her one-on-one — she needs tentacles and a landed E to win, so shove side lanes where she has few tentacles and your Maiden grinds her down."}],"wants":{"you":["Dodge Test of Spirit (E) and never fight in tentacle range","Body-block tentacle slams with ghouls and your wall","Split-push where she has few tentacles set up"],"foe":["Land Test of Spirit (E) to rip your Spirit and win the fight","Fight inside a dense tentacle field for max slam damage","Ult (R) with tentacles up to overwhelm your ghouls and heal"]},"early":"The early lane is a careful skill matchup — a farm race decided by dodging Test of Spirit (E) at 900 range. Harsh Lesson is her 4s leap and an auto reset, so the wind-up is your cue to step off, not the cast; soak the slams with ghouls.","mid":"It stays even through level 5 as long as you respect her E, then tips to you at 6: Maiden and ghouls tank her slams and out-DPS her, and your Dark Procession wall can cut off tentacles during her ult so they can't all connect.","late":"From first item onward you take over — ghouls plus Maiden out-sustain her healing and win extended trades, and one-on-one you out-split her since she needs a stacked tentacle field and a landed E to win, so shove side lanes where she has none.","whys":["Level 1 is an even, careful start decided entirely by dodging her E.","At level 2 it stays skill-based as both of you just farm and trade tentacle timings.","By level 3 it's still even so long as you avoid Test of Spirit.","Levels 4-5 remain a skill farm race with no clean kill for either side.","At level 6 you tip ahead — Maiden and ghouls tank slams and out-DPS her, and your wall cuts tentacles.","With first item your ghoul-and-Maiden sustain beats her healing in extended trades.","In the 2+ item stage you out-split her one-on-one, giving you the side lane."]},
  {"a":"yorick","b":"irelia","win":["Irelia","Irelia","Skill","Irelia","Skill","Irelia","Irelia"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 3-5","text":"Irelia uses your ghouls and minions as Bladesurge (Q) reset fuel to dash all over you, so hold your wall for when she's committed and don't clump ghouls where she can chain-Q through them."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Even with Maiden her Vanguard's Edge (R) wall plus stun sets up a full combo, so summon R only after she's used her ult or her Q dashes are exhausted."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Irelia's first item is a hard spike — Ionian Fervor stacks plus Bladesurge's heal-and-reset shred ghouls and out-sustain you, so buy Grievous Wounds and farm the wave."},{"when":"Late","text":"She out-duels you side-lane thanks to Q mobility and R disengage, so don't try to solo her — group and use ghouls plus Maiden as fight DPS she can't dash away from."}],"wants":{"you":["Deny Q resets — don't clump ghouls or let minions line up","Swing after Defiant Dance fires, never into it","Farm safely and avoid extended trades into her stacks"],"foe":["Chain Bladesurge (Q) resets off ghouls and minions","Stack passive for the shred-and-sustain spike","Use Vanguard's Edge (R) to wall, stun, and combo you"]},"early":"Irelia beats you early — her Bladesurge (Q) resets off your ghouls and minions let her dash around freely and out-trade you before you can wall, so farm carefully and don't feed her Q targets by clumping ghouls.","mid":"Level 3 is a brief skill window, but she reclaims it at 4-5 once her Q and passive come online; hold Dark Procession for when she's already dashed in, and keep ghouls spread so she can't chain-reset through them.","late":"From first item on she stays ahead — passive stacks plus Q resets shred your ghouls and out-sustain your trades, and her ult disengages your all-in, so stop dueling her, farm to relevance, and win by grouping where ghouls and Maiden add DPS she can't kite.","whys":["Irelia out-trades you at level 1 using Bladesurge resets off ghouls and minions.","At level 2 her Q mobility and stacking passive keep her ahead in every trade.","Level 3 is a brief skill window as your first ghouls and wall let you contest.","At levels 4-5 her online Q and passive reclaim control of the lane.","Level 6 is roughly even — your Maiden threatens but her R sets up a full combo.","With first item her stacks and Q resets shred ghouls and win extended trades.","In the 2+ item stage Irelia out-duels and out-kites you, owning the side lane."]},
  {"a":"yorick","b":"jax","win":["Jax","Jax","Skill","Skill","Skill","Jax","Jax"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 3-5","text":"Leap Strike (Q) plus Empower (W) gives him a burst combo that trades up on your slow autos. Dark Procession is terrain and stops the leap outright, so wall the ground between you rather than waiting out his 8s Q."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Both unlock ults, but Grandmaster-at-Arms (R) swings extended fights his way — every third attack adds magic damage and the active raises his resists. The stun is Counter Strike, 17s at rank 1, and it dodges basics while it runs."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Jax completing Blade of the Ruined King or Trinity Force outscales your single-item damage; keep Maiden shoving so you can leave lane rather than duel him head-on."},{"when":"Late","text":"Yorick is the better split-pusher here — Maiden plus ghouls take towers faster than Jax, so trade sides on the map and only fight him in the enemy jungle when Maiden is up."}],"wants":{"you":["Wall the ground he Leap Strikes over — Dark Procession is terrain and stops the leap","Keep Maiden and ghouls between you and Jax to soak his Counter Strike (E)","Shove and roam or take plates rather than straight-dueling him"],"foe":["Bait your Q/E, then Leap Strike (Q) in and dodge your slow autos behind Counter Strike (E)","Get to level 6 and 1-2 items to unlock his stun and dueling spike","Force sidelane 1v1s where Grandmaster-at-Arms resists blunt your ghouls"]},"early":"Jax owns levels 1-2: Leap Strike plus Empower out-trades your clunky autos before ghouls exist. Empower is an auto reset on 7s, so the wind-up is your cue to step back, not the cast.","mid":"Around 3-6 it evens out — Mourning Mist's slow kites his all-ins and Maiden wins you the wave. Counter Strike dodges basic attacks, so your whole ghoul pack whiffs into it: pull the swarm back for its duration, then swing.","late":"Once Jax hits Blade of the Ruined King/Trinity Force he wins the straight duel, so pivot to your strength: split with Maiden and ghouls, take towers he can't match, and only fight him when Maiden is active.","whys":["Jax's level-1 Leap Strike burst out-trades your slow melee autos before you have tools.","Jax's Empower + Q combo at level 2 continues to punish your weak early autos.","By level 3 your Mourning Mist slow lets you kite his all-in, evening the trade.","Ghouls and early Maiden let you contest the wave, keeping levels 4-5 even on skill.","Both ult at 6, so the fight comes down to positioning and cooldowns rather than a clear edge.","Jax's first item (BorK or Triforce) plus Grandmaster-at-Arms outscales your one-item damage.","Jax's fully-stacked ult resists shred your ghoul damage in extended 1v1s."]},
  {"a":"yorick","b":"jayce","win":["Jayce","Jayce","Skill","Jayce","Skill","Jayce","Yorick"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 3-5","text":"Jayce pokes you off the wave with Ranged form Shock Blast (Q) through the Acceleration Gate (E) — you can't reach him, so use ghouls and Maiden to sponge poke and only step up when his Q is on cooldown."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"His R is a 6s stance swap, and the first attack after swapping to Mercury Cannon cuts your armour and MR — that swap is the tell. The knockback is Thundering Blow (E); To the Skies! is the hammer leap."},{"when":"1st item","text":"A first-item Jayce (Manamune/Eclipse) still out-ranges and out-pokes you; keep the wave near your tower, farm with Q Last Rites, and heal on ghoul procs."},{"when":"Late","text":"By two items this row is yours: Maiden and ghouls shove towers Jayce can't defend alone, and To the Skies! is his only way into melee — Dark Procession is terrain and stops the leap. Avoid open-map poke lanes."}],"wants":{"you":["Use ghouls and Maiden as poke shields and to shove the wave under tower","Bait him into hammer form, then wall the ground To the Skies! leaps across and slow him","Farm safely with Q and look to out-split him rather than trade autos"],"foe":["Poke you down with Ranged Shock Blast (Q) through the Acceleration Gate (E) from max range","Zone you off cannon minions and deny your ghoul stacks","Keep the fight at range so you can never close the gap"]},"early":"Jayce dominates levels 1-2: his Ranged Shock Blast (Q) through Acceleration Gate (E) pokes you every time you step up for a last-hit, and you have no way to answer at that range.","mid":"It only levels out on the rare windows when his Q is down — then your ghouls and Maiden let you shove and heal; otherwise he keeps chunking you and level 6 gives him no ult but a strong form-swap burst.","late":"Jayce keeps the poke lead through his first item, but by two items the split is yours outright: Maiden and ghouls take towers he must answer alone, and inside hammer range the swarm beats him.","whys":["Jayce's level-1 Ranged Shock Blast out-ranges you and pokes freely.","Level-2 Acceleration Gate boosts his Q poke, keeping you off the wave.","On his Q cooldown windows your ghouls and Maiden even the wave state.","Jayce's form-swap poke chunks you every time you approach at level 4-5.","With no ult swing at 6, the fight stays skill-based around his cooldowns.","First-item Jayce out-pokes your single item and controls the lane.","By two items Maiden and ghouls siege towers Jayce cannot defend on his own."]},
  {"a":"yorick","b":"karma","win":["Karma","Karma","Skill","Yorick","Yorick","Yorick","Yorick"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 3-5","text":"Karma's empowered Inner Flame (Q via Mantra) plus Focused Resolve (W) root pokes and pins you, but her mana is thin — bait the W root, walk it out with Mourning Mist (E) slow on her, and punish the cooldown."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Karma has no traditional ult, just more Mantra charges, so 6 doesn't spike her; your Eulogy of the Isles (R) Maiden is the real power turn, giving you a body to shove and all-in through her shields."},{"when":"1st item","text":"After your first item and Maiden online, Yorick takes over — ghouls plus Maiden overwhelm Karma's single-target shielding and let you dive her under tower."},{"when":"Late","text":"Karma scales as a utility mage but can't 1v1 your ghoul army; keep Maiden shoving and force sidelane fights or picks where her Mantra-Q poke can't kite a full ghoul swarm."}],"wants":{"you":["Bait Focused Resolve (W) root, then close with Mourning Mist (E) slow and ghouls","Use Maiden and ghouls to overwhelm her single-target shields once you hit 6","Punish her thin mana pool by forcing repeated shove-and-trade cycles"],"foe":["Poke with Mantra-empowered Inner Flame (Q) and root you with Focused Resolve (W) early","Shield-and-kite your ghouls with Inspire (E) speed boosts","Keep the wave away and deny you all-in windows before your Maiden is up"]},"early":"Karma edges level 1: her Inner Flame (Q) out-ranges your melee autos and Focused Resolve (W) can root you for chip damage before you have ghouls to trade back.","mid":"From level 2 through 5 it's even and skill-based — her poke and shields balance against your ghoul stacking and Mourning Mist (E) slow, and her thin mana means she can't spam without going empty.","late":"Level 6 is your swing: Maiden plus a full ghoul line overwhelm Karma's single-target shielding, so all-in her under tower with your first item and then split, since she can't 1v1 the swarm.","whys":["Karma's level-1 Inner Flame poke and W root out-range your melee before you have ghouls.","At 2 she still out-ranges you — Inner Flame chips while your ghoul count is thin.","Mourning Mist at 3 evens it: the mark slows her and ghouls leap on it.","Levels 4-5 stay even — her shields answer your ghouls without a clear edge.","Karma has no level-6 spike; Maiden floods a wave her single Q cannot clear.","Your Maiden and first item overwhelm her single-target shields for a Yorick all-in.","Late, her utility scaling and your split roughly balance into a skill matchup."]},
  {"a":"yorick","b":"kassadin","win":["Yorick","Yorick","Yorick","Yorick","Yorick","Yorick","Kassadin"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 3-5","text":"Kassadin is weak and melee-ranged pre-6 against magic-less you — his Null Sphere (Q) shield blocks some ghoul poke but he can't trade, so shove hard, deny farm, and stack Maiden charges to set up an early lead."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"This is your window: before Riftwalk (R) snowballs, use Eulogy of the Isles (R) Maiden plus Mourning Mist (E) slow to all-in and burst him — a kill or two here delays his scaling and is your whole gameplan."},{"when":"1st item","text":"With Maiden up and a first item you can still dive Kassadin, but his Rod of Ages/Catalyst stacks are ticking; end the lane fast or shove and take his tower before he comes online."},{"when":"Late","text":"Once Kassadin has items and Riftwalk stacks he blinks around your ghouls and one-shots squishies — you can't catch him, so your only answer is to split hard with Maiden and end before he takes over teamfights."}],"wants":{"you":["Shove and deny farm pre-6 while Kassadin is weak and melee","All-in at 6 with Maiden + Mourning Mist (E) slow before Riftwalk snowballs","Take his tower and force his tempo down before he scales"],"foe":["Survive lane with Null Sphere (Q) shield and hit item + level spikes","Use Riftwalk (R) to dodge your ghouls and Mourning Mist (E)","Scale into the mid-game where he blinks around and bursts your team"]},"early":"Levels 1-5 are skill-based but favour aggression: Kassadin is a weak melee laner with no magic damage to fear from you, so shove, deny his farm, and build a lead while he's helpless.","mid":"Level 6 is your peak — before Riftwalk (R) starts snowballing, Maiden plus your Mourning Mist (E) slow lets you all-in and burst him, and a kill here sets his whole game back.","late":"The clock is against you: once Kassadin stacks items and Riftwalk charges he blinks around your ghouls and deletes squishies, so split-push with Maiden and close the game before he takes over.","whys":["Level 1 is yours — he has one 650-range Q and cannot answer a melee step-up.","At 2 your ghouls arrive and he has no wave clear — shove and deny him.","Mourning Mist at 3 out-ranges his 650 Q and his shield eats only magic.","Levels 4-5 stay yours — deny farm and set up the level-6 all-in.","At 6 your Maiden and E slow let you all-in before Riftwalk snowballs.","With Maiden and first item you can still dive him before he scales.","Late, Kassadin's Riftwalk mobility and burst outscale you completely."]},
  {"a":"yorick","b":"kayle","win":["Yorick","Yorick","Yorick","Yorick","Skill","Yorick","Yorick"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 3-5","text":"Kayle is one of the weakest early laners in the game — melee-ranged and no waveclear — so slam the wave into her, deny CS with ghouls, and stack Maiden charges; every minute she's behind delays her powerspikes."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Her Divine Judgment (R) invulnerability is only single-target and short, but she still can't fight you — use Eulogy of the Isles (R) Maiden plus Mourning Mist (E) slow to all-in and keep her off the wave."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Yorick stays firmly ahead: your Maiden and ghouls out-DPS a Kayle who's still stacking toward her ranged form, so dive her tower and take plates to snowball her out of the game."},{"when":"Late","text":"Kayle's only path back is scaling to a hyper-carry, so you must end fast — split with Maiden, take towers she can't defend, and force the game to close before her 11/16 ranged and true-damage spikes arrive."}],"wants":{"you":["Shove and deny CS relentlessly while Kayle is weak and melee","All-in at 6 with Maiden + Mourning Mist (E) slow to keep her behind","Take towers and end the game before her late-game scaling arrives"],"foe":["Farm safely with Radiant Blast (Q) poke and survive to level spikes","Use Divine Judgment (R) to negate your all-in damage","Reach her ranged form and hyper-carry into the late game"]},"early":"Levels 1-5 are skill-based on paper but heavily aggression-favoured: Kayle is a helpless melee laner with weak waveclear, so shove into her, deny farm, and build the lead that keeps her from scaling.","mid":"Level 6 tips clearly to you — even with Divine Judgment (R) as a single-target lifeline, she can't answer your Maiden plus Mourning Mist (E) all-in, so pressure her off every wave.","late":"You must convert before she comes online: keep Maiden shoving and take towers she can't hold, ending the game before her ranged form and true damage make her a hyper-carry.","whys":["Level 1 is even, but Kayle's weakness lets you set up early shove pressure.","Level 2 stays skill-based as you shove and she farms defensively.","Level 3 remains even while you deny CS and stack Maiden.","Levels 4-5 are still skill-based as you build your 6 all-in.","At 6 your Maiden and E slow overwhelm her single-target R, favouring you.","First-item Maiden and ghouls out-DPS a still-scaling Kayle.","You hold the lead late as long as you end before her hyper-carry spike."]},
  {"a":"yorick","b":"kennen","win":["Skill","Kennen","Kennen","Yorick","Kennen","Kennen","Yorick"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 3-5","text":"Kennen ranges you down with Thundering Shuriken (Q) and can stun you with a Lightning Rush (E) + Q mark stack; use ghouls and Maiden to soak poke and don't step up while his Q is up."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Slicing Maelstrom (R) doesn't win a 1v1 outright, but combined with a jungler it's a guaranteed stun-lock — respect roams and don't overextend when his ult is up."},{"when":"1st item","text":"A first-item Kennen (Hextech Rocketbelt/Liandry's) keeps poking you out of lane and stacking his passive stuns; farm safely with Q Last Rites and heal on ghoul procs."},{"when":"Late","text":"Yorick's out is the split — Maiden and ghouls take towers Kennen can't hold alone, so avoid grouped fights where his AoE ult and stun chain shine and trade sides on the map instead."}],"wants":{"you":["Use ghouls and Maiden to shield against Thundering Shuriken (Q) poke","Farm with Q under tower and heal off ghoul procs when poked low","Split with Maiden rather than grouping into his AoE ult"],"foe":["Poke you down with ranged Thundering Shuriken (Q) from safety","Stack passive marks via Lightning Rush (E) to stun and burst you","Group for teamfights where Slicing Maelstrom (R) locks your team down"]},"early":"Kennen owns levels 1-2: his ranged Thundering Shuriken (Q) chips you every time you go for a last-hit and you have no way to trade back at that range yet.","mid":"It evens out around 3-5 once you have ghouls and Maiden to soak poke and shove — his stun combo is scary but predictable, so play around his Q cooldown and don't stack marks.","late":"Kennen's poke and AoE stun keep him ahead in lane and fights, so your answer is the split: Maiden and ghouls pressure towers he can't defend, letting you win the map while avoiding his grouped ult.","whys":["Even at 1 — his Q costs 60 mana and he cannot commit to a trade.","Level-2 Q + E mark stacking lets him stun-trade you down.","By level 3 ghouls and Maiden soak his poke, evening the lane.","Levels 4-5 swing to you: Mourning Mist is 700 range and shreds armour.","At 6 his ult needs a gank to win 1v1, keeping the lane even.","First-item Kennen out-pokes your single item and keeps you off the wave.","Your split wins the map — Maiden takes towers his 120s ult can't defend."]},
  {"a":"yorick","b":"kled","win":["Kled","Kled","Kled","Kled","Kled","Kled","Yorick"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 3-5","text":"Kled's Bear Trap on a Rope (Q) pull plus Violent Tendencies (W) attack-speed steroid lets him win every early trade while mounted; don't stand in Q range, and use Mourning Mist (E) slow to peel away when he all-ins."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Chaaaaaaaarge!!! (R) gives him engage and a shield, and his dismount burst can straight kill you early; use Dark Procession (W) wall and E slow to survive the all-in and don't fight while he's mounted with W up."},{"when":"1st item","text":"A first-item Kled still out-duels you, but the fight tightens — bait his skirmish, then remount denial: keep him unmounted by kiting with ghouls and E, since dismounted Kled is far weaker."},{"when":"Late","text":"This is where Yorick takes over — Maiden and ghouls out-split Kled and out-DPS him in a sustained fight, so play for the late split, take his towers, and only fight when Maiden is up."}],"wants":{"you":["Avoid Bear Trap (Q) range and kite his mounted Violent Tendencies (W) window","Use Dark Procession (W) wall + Mourning Mist (E) slow to survive his all-in","Play for the late split where Maiden and ghouls out-DPS him"],"foe":["Land Bear Trap (Q) to pull you in and burst while mounted","Use Violent Tendencies (W) and Chaaaaaaaarge!!! (R) to win early all-ins","Snowball the early lead before your Maiden scaling comes online"]},"early":"Kled dominates levels 1-4: his Bear Trap (Q) pull and Violent Tendencies (W) steroid win every mounted trade, and his dismount burst can outright kill you, so respect Q range and farm defensively.","mid":"It only starts to even around 5-6 once you have ghouls, Maiden, and Mourning Mist (E) to kite him — survive his Chaaaaaaaarge!!! (R) all-in with your Dark Procession (W) wall and don't duel while he's mounted.","late":"The matchup flips late: Maiden and a full ghoul line out-split and out-DPS Kled in sustained fights, so scale, take his towers, and pick fights only when Maiden is active.","whys":["Kled's level-1 mounted trade with W steroid beats your weak early autos.","Level-2 Bear Trap (Q) pull lets him burst you before you can answer.","At level 3 his all-in with W and Q still out-trades your ghouls.","Kled keeps the lead through 4 with his dismount burst threat.","At 6 his Chaaaaaaaarge!!! adds engage and a shield — still his lane.","First-item Kled still out-duels you; the fight tightens but stays his.","Late, Maiden and ghouls out-split and out-DPS him for the Yorick edge."]},
  {"a":"yorick","b":"ksante","win":["Yorick","Skill","Skill","K'Sante","Yorick","Yorick","K'Sante"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 3-5","text":"At 4 K'Sante gets his second Ntofo Strikes charge and can chain-stun you into a wall, so respect the range on his rock throw and don't E in when both charges are up."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Your R lands first as a fight-swinger: drop the Maiden and the wraiths shred K'Sante while he's stuck deciding whether to All Out. His R only reformats his stats, it doesn't clear your ghouls."},{"when":"1st item","text":"With Tiamat plus a few ghouls up you win the extended trade every time; his base Ntofo damage is low and he leans on burst-then-reset that your cage (W) shuts down."},{"when":"Late","text":"Full-build K'Sante in All Out becomes a true diver who ignores your cage's slow and flings you out of position, so late skirmishes tilt back to him if he catches you without Maiden."}],"wants":{"you":["Poke him down with Q auto-resets while ghouls tank his Ntofo","Fight on top of a full Maiden + wraith wall","Freeze so his short-range engage overextends him into your ghouls"],"foe":["Wall-stun you with Ntofo Strikes then All Out to reset the fight","Use R to knock you out of your ghoul stack and cage","Roam or teamfight where his displacement matters more than your DoT"]},"early":"You out-trade the early levels: your Q resets heal and cleave while his Ntofo poke is weak before charges, so bully him and deny the wall setups.","mid":"Once he hits 4 his double-charge wall combo can lock you, but your level 6 Maiden flips extended fights hard in your favour since wraiths ignore his shields.","late":"After first item you keep the split and win 1v1s, but full-build All Out K'Sante out-duels you if he R's you off your ghouls in a straight teamfight.","whys":["You win Level 1 because your Q reset trade and heal beat his weak pre-charge Ntofo poke.","Level 2 is skill: his first Ntofo charge lets him poke back, evening the trade.","Level 3 is even as both hit power-item timings with no hard advantage yet.","At 4-5 K'Sante's second Ntofo charge enables the wall-stun chain, tilting the window his way.","Your Level 6 Maiden and wraith wall flip the fight since they shred through his shields.","First item favours you as Tiamat plus ghouls win every extended trade against his low base damage.","With two items All Out K'Sante becomes a reset diver who R's you off your stack, so late goes to him."]},
  {"a":"yorick","b":"lillia","win":["Lillia","Lillia","Skill","Skill","Lillia","Lillia","Lillia"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 3-5","text":"Lillia kites your ghouls with her Q spin and Blooming Blows passive move-speed, so she pokes you and the ghouls apart before you can commit an E-mark trade."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Her R Lullaby is the real threat: it drowsies you and forces a sleep, then she full-combos while you can't move. Don't fight near her when Lullaby is up unless you have Maiden pressure."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Once she stacks move-speed and buys AP she out-DPS's your ghouls and simply runs away from your E slow, kiting the wave and out-poking the trade."},{"when":"Late","text":"Late Lillia is a mobile magic-DoT threat who whittles your Maiden and ghouls from range and disengages your cage entirely, so she keeps winning the extended fight."}],"wants":{"you":["Freeze the wave so she can't kite in open space","Land E to mark her and stick with ghouls before her move-speed ramps","Split-push and pressure sidelanes where her poke matters less"],"foe":["Kite ghouls with Q spin and Blooming Blows move-speed","Land R Lullaby to sleep you then burst","Poke you and ghouls apart from max range and disengage"]},"early":"Lillia edges the early levels: her Q passive move-speed lets her poke you while dancing around your ghouls, so play safe and last-hit rather than chasing.","mid":"You reach a skill window around 3-4 where a clean E-mark can catch her, but her level 6 Lullaby swings it back as a guaranteed sleep-and-burst.","late":"After items her AP DoT out-damages your ghouls and her mobility ignores your E slow and W cage, so the extended fight stays hers.","whys":["Lillia wins Level 1 with Blooming Blows move-speed poke that kites you and your lone ghoul.","Level 2 stays hers as the extra Q ramp lets her dance out of every trade you start.","Level 3 is skill: a landed E mark lets you stick and even the trade briefly.","Levels 4-5 are even as you both hit spike timings and neither commits cleanly.","Her Level 6 Lullaby drowsy-sleep guarantees a full burst combo on you.","First item favours Lillia as AP plus move-speed lets her out-poke and run from your slow.","Late she out-DoTs your ghouls and disengages your cage, keeping the fight hers."]},
  {"a":"yorick","b":"lucian","win":["Lucian","Lucian","Lucian","Skill","Skill","Yorick","Yorick"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 3-5","text":"Lucian's Q through a minion and W-into-passive double-tap chunks you hard, and his E dash dodges your E mark, so he wins every short trade at range before your ghouls arrive."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"His R Culling is heavy sustained damage, but your Maiden actually helps here: drop it so wraiths body-block and soak the beam while you cage him. This is your least-bad fight window."},{"when":"1st item","text":"With his lane kit online Lucian pokes you off the wave and uses E to reposition out of every ghoul swarm, keeping the poke war one-sided."},{"when":"Late","text":"Late Lucian is a hyper-mobile marksman who out-ranges your Maiden and dashes your cage, so he keeps kiting your ghouls and winning the extended fight."}],"wants":{"you":["Stack ghouls and force him to fight in melee range","Land E when his E dash is on cooldown","Push and roam so his weak wave-clear falls behind"],"foe":["Poke with Q-through-minion and W passive double-tap","Dodge your E and disengage ghouls with his E dash","Kite the ghoul swarm from range and out-trade with Culling"]},"early":"Lucian bullies the early levels: his Q and passive double-tap out-poke you and his E dash sidesteps your E mark, so soak XP and don't chase.","mid":"There's a skill window at 3 and 5 where a landed E lets you close with ghouls, but his level 6 kit and dash keep most trades in his favour.","late":"After items his range and mobility out-class your Maiden and cage, so the poke war and extended fight both stay his.","whys":["Lucian wins Level 1 with his Q-through-minion and passive double-tap poke before ghouls exist.","Level 2 stays his as the W-passive combo chunks you and his E dodges your commit.","Level 3 is skill: a landed E mark lets you stick briefly and even a trade.","Levels 4-5 favour Lucian as his poke and E dash keep out-trading your ghoul swarm.","Level 6 is even because your Maiden soaks Culling and gives your best fight window.","First item is yours: Maiden plus the swarm out-damages his poke in a brawl.","Late your split wins — Maiden takes side towers a lone marksman cannot hold."]},
  {"a":"yorick","b":"malphite","win":["Skill","Yorick","Yorick","Skill","Yorick","Yorick","Malphite"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 3-5","text":"Malphite's only trade tool is Q slow plus Thunderlord-style passive-shield E, and it's weak into your Q reset healing, so you win extended trades once ghouls are up around 4."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"His R is a teamfight engage, not a duel button, so in lane your Maiden simply overwhelms him; drop it and his passive shield melts under wraith and ghoul focus."},{"when":"1st item","text":"With Tiamat and ghouls you shove him under tower and dive; his mana pool is tiny and his E armour-shred hurts your ghouls but not enough to stop the swarm."},{"when":"Late","text":"Late Malphite builds full armour/HP and holds his R for your carries; his unstoppable teamfight ult and tankiness let him ignore your split and win the 5v5, tilting late to him."}],"wants":{"you":["Fight extended once ghouls are up and out-sustain his weak poke","Shove and dive him under tower with Maiden","Keep pressure sidelane before his R teamfight matters"],"foe":["Save mana and poke only with Q slow","Hold R for a teamfight engage on your carries","Stack armour and out-tank your ghouls in the 5v5"]},"early":"You control the early levels: your Q reset healing out-sustains his weak Q-poke and low mana, so trade freely and stack a lead.","mid":"From level 4 through first item you dominate the extended fight, your Maiden and ghouls overwhelm his passive shield and shove him off the wave.","late":"Late Malphite scales into a full-tank teamfight engage whose R decides fights your split can't, so the 5v5 tilts back to him.","whys":["You win Level 1 as your Q reset trade and heal beat his weak Q-slow poke.","Level 2 is skill as his passive-shield E gives him one even trade window.","Level 3 stays even before your ghoul swarm fully comes online.","At 4-5 your ghouls and sustain overwhelm his low-mana poke in extended trades.","Your Level 6 Maiden overwhelms him since his R is engage, not a duel button.","First item favours you as Tiamat plus ghouls shove and dive his tiny mana pool.","Late full-tank Malphite's R teamfight engage out-values your split, tilting to him."]},
  {"a":"yorick","b":"maokai","win":["Yorick","Skill","Skill","Yorick","Yorick","Yorick","Skill"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 3-5","text":"Maokai's W root plus Q sapling poke is his whole kit, and his mana runs dry fast; your Q reset healing out-sustains it, so you win the extended trade once ghouls join around 4."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"His R is a slow teamfight wave, useless in a duel, so your Maiden simply out-fights him in lane; drop it and the wraiths chew through his passive sustain."},{"when":"1st item","text":"With Tiamat and ghouls you shove and dive; his W root can still peel one ghoul rotation but his damage is too low to stop the swarm from killing him."},{"when":"Late","text":"Late Maokai is a full-tank engage support with a global-threat R and heavy CC for teamfights; his utility out-values your split, so the 5v5 late-game evens out."}],"wants":{"you":["Fight extended once ghouls are up and out-sustain his poke","Shove and dive with Maiden while his mana is low","Freeze so his short W root can't trade safely"],"foe":["Land W root then Q sapling poke and disengage","Save R for a teamfight engage, not the duel","Peel ghouls with root and scale into a tanky CC bot"]},"early":"You win the early levels: your Q reset healing out-sustains his sapling poke and his mana empties fast, so trade freely and deny him.","mid":"From 4 through first item you dominate the extended fight, your Maiden and ghoul swarm out-DPS his weak damage and shove him off the wave.","late":"Late Maokai becomes a full-tank teamfight engage whose R and CC out-value your split, so the 5v5 late-game levels back to even.","whys":["You win Level 1 as your Q reset trade and heal out-sustain his sapling poke.","Level 2 is skill: his W root gives him one even trade window.","Level 3 stays even before your ghoul swarm is fully online.","At 4-5 your ghouls and sustain overwhelm his low-mana poke in extended trades.","Your Level 6 Maiden out-fights him since his R is a teamfight wave, not a duel.","First item favours you as Tiamat plus ghouls shove and dive his weak damage.","Late full-tank Maokai's R and CC utility out-value your split, evening the 5v5."]},
  {"a":"yorick","b":"mel","win":["Skill","Mel","Mel","Mel","Skill","Yorick","Yorick"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 3-5","text":"Mel is a ranged mage who pokes with her Q barrage and Overwhelm-stacked autos; early she out-ranges you, so soak XP behind ghouls and don't walk into free poke."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Her R is a delayed execute nuke, so respect low-HP thresholds, but this is where you flip it: E-mark her, cage with W, and the ghoul swarm plus Maiden closes the gap she can't kite."},{"when":"1st item","text":"With Tiamat and a full ghoul stack you out-sustain and all-in through her poke; her W reflect can turn one ability but not the whole swarm, and she's squishy when caged."},{"when":"Late","text":"Late Mel can burst from range and her W Rebuttal reflects your engage, so if she gets peel she out-damages you at distance; without peel your split still wins the map."}],"wants":{"you":["Cage her with W and all-in through the poke with ghouls","Land E to close the gap her poke relies on","Split-push and dive her squishy frame under tower"],"foe":["Poke with Q barrage and Overwhelm autos from range","Reflect your engage ability with W Rebuttal","Land R execute on your low-HP threshold"]},"early":"Mel out-ranges you early: her Q barrage and stacked autos poke you off the wave, so play safe behind ghouls and farm for your spikes.","mid":"The mid-levels are a skill window where a landed E lets you close, then your level 6 Maiden all-in overwhelms her squishy caged frame.","late":"Rebuttal blanks a raw Mourning Mist on a 26s cooldown, so cage first and mark after; one bubble never stops a full Walker swarm on the side lane.","whys":["Level 1 is even: Radiant Volley chips, but Last Rites heals every 6s to answer it.","Level 2 is Mel's: Solar Snare roots on 11s and her Q follows it in.","Level 3 stays even while you stack ghouls out of her range.","Levels 4-5 stay Mel's: her poke scales faster than your grave stacking.","Level 6 evens: Eulogy of the Isles raises Walkers against her Golden Eclipse.","First item favours you — Dark Procession on 16s cages her frame for the swarm.","Late favours you: Rebuttal blanks one spell, never the whole Walker swarm."]},
  {"a":"yorick","b":"mordekaiser","win":["Skill","Mordekaiser","Mordekaiser","Mordekaiser","Mordekaiser","Skill","Yorick"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 3-5","text":"Once Morde has Q and E he pulls you in with E, lands the empowered Q swing, and his passive Indestructible shield out-sustains your ghoul trade, so he wins extended fights from 2 onward."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"His R Realm of Death is the whole matchup: he banishes you 1v1, leaves your Maiden and ghouls behind, and duels you alone where you're weakest. Never fight with R up unless you can flash the E pull."},{"when":"1st item","text":"With a first item his passive shield and DoT out-heal your ghoul chip, and his R keeps isolating you from the swarm that is your only advantage."},{"when":"Late","text":"Late Morde stacks the death realm, magic pen, and shield into an unbeatable 1v1 that strips your ghosts on entry, so the extended fight and the split duel both stay his."}],"wants":{"you":["Win the level 1 all-in before his shield and pull come online","Fight only with full Maiden and ghouls stacked, never isolated","Push and cross-map so his R can't catch you alone"],"foe":["Pull you in with E and land empowered Q for the shield","Banish you with R away from your ghouls and Maiden","Out-sustain the ghoul swarm with his Indestructible passive"]},"early":"You own level 1, your Q reset all-in beats him before his shield and E pull exist, so front-load damage while you can.","mid":"From level 2 onward Morde takes over: his E-Q combo and passive shield out-trade you, and level 6 R isolates you from the ghouls you depend on.","late":"Realm of Death takes you alone every 100s and leaves Maiden outside, but that is one duel — on the side lane with it down, your split still wins.","whys":["Level 1 is even: Last Rites resets your auto, but Darkness Rise arms after 3 hits.","Morde takes Level 2 with the E-pull-into-Q combo and Indestructible shield.","Level 3 is his: a free Obliterate every 6s outdamages your grave chip.","At 4-5 his E-Q shield trade out-sustains your ghoul chip, favouring him.","Level 6 is his: Realm of Death drags you off the swarm for a solo duel.","First item evens once Executioner's Calling cuts the Indestructible heal.","Late is yours: Realm of Death is one 100s duel, your split runs all game."]},
  {"a":"yorick","b":"nasus","win":["Skill","Skill","Skill","Skill","Yorick","Yorick","Yorick"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 3-5","text":"You can freely E-poke Nasus off the cannon wave; his Q Siphoning Strike does nothing to your maiden trades and he has no way to punish you back until he has stacks."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Your R Eulogy of the Isles arrives before his ult matters much on cooldown; a Maiden dive turns his farm phase into a defensive crouch under tower and starves his Q stacks."},{"when":"1st item","text":"With Tiamat/Bami and Maiden pushing, you cut Nasus off from CS entirely; every wave you deny is a Siphoning Strike stack he never gets."},{"when":"Late","text":"Even a fed Nasus can't 1v1 your Maiden-plus-ghouls DPS through his W slow window, and you out-splitpush a champion who only wants to farm."}],"wants":{"you":["Perma-shove with Maiden so Nasus farms under tower","E to trade and clear ranged minions before his Q","Roam or dive once R is up while he's frozen on CS"],"foe":["A calm free-farm lane to stack Siphoning Strike","To W-slow you and land a big empowered Q","To scale past 200-300 stacks into teamfights"]},"early":"Levels 1-2 are neutral pushing and last-hits; neither of you threatens a kill and Nasus just wants to touch minions while you set up your wave.","mid":"From 3 onward you own the lane: E Mourning Mist plus Maiden shreds Nasus in every extended trade, and by 6 your ult lets you dive or shove him off farm so his Q stacks stall out.","late":"You keep the splitpush lead with ghouls and Maiden; the only danger is letting him free-stack, so keep his CS starved and the game stays yours.","whys":["Level 1 is an even farm-and-position phase with no kill threat for either side.","Level 2 stays skill-based; Nasus has no engage and you have no all-in yet.","Level 3 is still roughly even as you begin E-poking but can't commit a kill.","Levels 4-5 remain a neutral farming standoff before your ult swings it.","At 6 your Maiden and R let you dive and starve his stacks, tilting it to you.","With your first item and Maiden shoving, you deny his farm and out-trade him.","With 2+ items you out-splitpush and out-DPS Nasus, keeping the lead."]},
  {"a":"yorick","b":"nautilus","win":["Yorick","Nautilus","Nautilus","Nautilus","Yorick","Yorick","Yorick"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 3-5","text":"Respect Nautilus level 4 with W Titan's Wrath shield up plus Q Dredge Line hook; his passive root chains your movement and lets him unload point-blank on you."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Your R Eulogy of the Isles flips the fight; even if he Q-hooks in, Maiden and ghouls out-sustain his shielded burst and he has no escape once committed."},{"when":"1st item","text":"With Tiamat and Maiden you shove Nautilus in and win any trade he starts, since he has no wave sustain and can't duel your ghoul wall."},{"when":"Late","text":"Nautilus falls off to a pure engage-support role; you out-splitpush and out-scale a tank who can't stop your Maiden from taking towers."}],"wants":{"you":["Trade at level 1 with E before his shield comes online","Cage his retreat, never terrain he can hook to escape","Shove and dive once R and Maiden are up"],"foe":["Level 4 all-in with W shield and Q-passive-Q chain CC","To land a hook and burst you before you can peel","To roam bot and gank with his heavy lockdown"]},"early":"Level 1 favors you: E Mourning Mist plus an auto out-trades Nautilus before his W Titan's Wrath shield is available, so poke him early.","mid":"Level 4 is his window with shield and the Q-passive-Q CC chain, so play back there; but by 6 your ult, Maiden and ghouls overpower his shielded all-in and you reclaim control.","late":"You out-scale and out-splitpush a pure engage tank; keep waves shoving and take towers with Maiden while he can't 1v1 you.","whys":["Level 1 is yours because E and an auto beat Nautilus before his shield exists.","Level 2 is his: Dredge Line hooks at 1150 range and Titan's Wrath is up.","Level 3 stays his while Riptide slows you every 7s.","Level 4 favors Nautilus: W shield plus Q-passive-Q chain CC lets him burst you.","At 6 your R and Maiden overpower his shielded all-in, flipping it to you.","With your first item and Maiden you shove and win trades he can't sustain.","With 2+ items you out-scale and out-splitpush the falling-off tank."]},
  {"a":"yorick","b":"neeko","win":["Skill","Neeko","Neeko","Neeko","Neeko","Neeko","Yorick"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 3-5","text":"Neeko out-pokes you hard early with Q Blooming Burst double-hitting your minion clump and E Tangle-Barbs rooting you; her passive lets her hide as a minion to bait bad E's out of you."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Pop Blossom's wind-up is hidden while she is disguised, so a lone minion walking at you is the tell; survive the pop and cage her escape."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Trades even out as your Maiden pushes; she can still burst but can't stop your wave, so you start pressuring her under tower."},{"when":"Late","text":"Neeko is a teamfight burst mage with no splitpush answer; your Maiden and ghouls take towers and side-lane duels she can't contest."}],"wants":{"you":["Dodge her E Tangle-Barbs to deny the root-into-Q burst","Cage her retreat once Pop Blossom has been spent","Out-splitpush her once items and Maiden are online"],"foe":["Early Q Blooming Burst poke and E roots to zone you off CS","Passive minion disguise to bait your E and set up burst","Level 6 Pop Blossom all-in with Flash or a gank"]},"early":"Levels 1-3 are Neeko's: Q Blooming Burst chunks you through the wave and E Tangle-Barbs roots you for free poke while her passive disguise baits your cooldowns, so play safe and farm.","mid":"Around 4-6 the lane levels out; her R Pop Blossom is scary but you survive it with Maiden and ghouls and can wall the follow-up, so respect the all-in without conceding CS.","late":"You take over: Neeko has no splitpush and can't stop your Maiden, so you out-scale into side-lane pressure and towers.","whys":["Level 1 is even: Blooming Burst costs 50 mana and she has no root yet.","Level 2 stays hers with double-Q burst and disguise mind-games.","Level 3 is still Neeko's off E-into-Q poke that zones you from CS.","Levels 4-5 stay hers: Tangle-Barbs roots at 1000 range every 10s.","Level 6 is hers: Pop Blossom knocks up and stuns, hidden while disguised.","First item still hers — her burst leads your chip until you can split.","With 2+ items you out-splitpush the burst mage who can't answer Maiden."]},
  {"a":"yorick","b":"olaf","win":["Olaf","Olaf","Olaf","Olaf","Olaf","Olaf","Yorick"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 3-5","text":"Undertow is a 1000-range axe on a flat 9s and picking it back up resets the cooldown, so he perma-slows and chases; Reckless Swing adds true damage at 325 range on 11s that armour cannot stop."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Ragnarok makes him immune to disables, so Mourning Mist's slow does nothing — but Dark Procession is terrain, not CC, and the cage still holds him."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Berserker Rage gives attack speed and lifesteal as his health drops, so the longer the duel runs the harder he wins it — never extend."},{"when":"Late","text":"Ragnarok is 80s at rank 3 and only holds while he keeps attacking — take the side lane, not the duel, and Maiden takes the tower for you."}],"wants":{"you":["Kite his axe pickups and never fight when Q slow is on you","Use ghouls and Maiden to soak his E while you disengage","Splitpush and cross-map rather than duel him head-on"],"foe":["Land Q Undertow, pick up the axe, and perma-slow-chase you","R Ragnarok to shrug off your slow and all-in through it","Stack lifesteal and out-sustain your trades"]},"early":"Levels 1-2 are Olaf's: his Q axe slow and E Reckless Swing chunk you in any trade, and with W lifesteal he sustains through your E poke, so give ground.","mid":"He stays ahead through 3-6; Ragnarok strips your slow by making him immune to disables, but it is not a wall-breaker — Dark Procession still cages him, so save it for his commit.","late":"Olaf out-duels you 1v1, but Ragnarok is 80s at rank 3 and answers only disables — split with Maiden and take the towers he cannot defend alone.","whys":["Level 1 favors Olaf as his Q axe and E out-trade your early poke.","Level 2 stays his with axe pickups perma-slowing and chasing you.","Level 3 stays his: Undertow's cooldown resets when he retrieves the axe.","Level 4 stays Olaf's: Berserker Rage gives lifesteal as his health drops.","Level 6 is his: Ragnarok makes him immune to disables while he swings.","With first item Olaf's lifesteal and axe out-duel your Maiden trades.","Two-plus items: your split takes towers he cannot defend."]},
  {"a":"yorick","b":"ornn","win":["Yorick","Skill","Ornn","Ornn","Ornn","Ornn","Yorick"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 3-5","text":"Ornn's level 4 is real: Bellows Breath applies Brittle, and Volcanic Rupture leaves a magma pillar he can Searing Charge into for a knock-up — never overstay inside a trade."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Call of the Forge God travels 2500 range, slows and applies Brittle, and he can recast to charge into it and redirect — the level 6 window is his, not yours."},{"when":"1st item","text":"With Tiamat and Maiden you perma-shove and deny Ornn's CS and forge tempo, out-pressuring a tank who only scales."},{"when":"Late","text":"Ornn out-scales into teamfights: his upgraded items, R Call of the Forge God knock-up and brittle combo make him tanky and hard to burst in the 1v1."}],"wants":{"you":["Trade at level 1 with E before his brittle combo is online","Shove with Maiden to deny his farm and forge timings","Use R and ghouls to dive him off CS mid-game"],"foe":["Level 4 W Bellows Breath brittle knock-up to punish your trades","Q Volcanic Rupture pillar plus E charging into it","Scale to full items and out-tank you in the late 1v1"]},"early":"Level 1 is yours: E Mourning Mist plus an auto out-trades Ornn before his W and brittle combo exist, so poke him and set up the wave.","mid":"Respect his level-4 spike where W Bellows Breath and a wall-slam brittle can chunk you, but from 5-6 your Maiden, R and ghouls let you shove him off farm and deny his forge tempo.","late":"Ornn out-scales you late: upgraded items plus his R knock-up and brittle make him tanky and tough to kill 1v1, so bank your mid-game splitpush lead before that.","whys":["Level 1 is yours as E and an auto beat Ornn before his brittle exists.","Level 2 is even while he builds toward his level-4 power spike.","Level 3 stays skill-based just before his W brittle combo comes online.","Level 4 favors Ornn: W Bellows Breath brittle knock-up punishes trades.","Level 6 is his: Call of the Forge God slows and makes you Brittle.","With first item and Maiden you deny his CS and forge tempo.","Two-plus items: your split takes towers he must answer alone."]},
  {"a":"yorick","b":"pantheon","win":["Pantheon","Pantheon","Pantheon","Yorick","Pantheon","Yorick","Yorick"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 3-5","text":"Early Pantheon is brutal: Comet Spear pokes on 11s and Shield Vault dashes in stunning on 13s as an auto reset — the wind-up is your cue to step back, not the cast."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Grand Starfall leaps from 5500 range on 180s and lands slowing — it is a map tool, and at 6 he can be anywhere, so hold the wave near your tower."},{"when":"1st item","text":"With Tiamat and Maiden you out-sustain Pantheon's poke and shove him in; he falls off hard once you have HP and a ghoul wall to soak his combo."},{"when":"Late","text":"Pantheon becomes a squishy early-game bully with no scaling; you out-splitpush, out-duel and out-tower a champion who's out of gas."}],"wants":{"you":["Survive the level 1-3 poke and freeze/farm safely","Cage his retreat once Shield Vault has been spent","Out-scale with Maiden and shove him off the map"],"foe":["Q Comet Spear plus W Shield Vault stun to all-in you early","Mortal Will to empower his next spell","Snowball the first three levels before you spike"]},"early":"Levels 1-3 are all Pantheon: Comet Spear pokes on 11s and Shield Vault dashes in with a stun on 13s, and it resets his auto, so the wind-up is the tell. Play defensive and give CS if you must.","mid":"Level 4 flips it as your ghoul swarm soaks his combo — but Aegis Assault is invulnerable from the front on 22s, so mark him and bring the swarm in behind it.","late":"You take over completely: Pantheon has no scaling, so you out-sustain, out-splitpush and out-tower a champion who's now just a squishy early bully.","whys":["Level 1 favors Pantheon with Q poke and W stun all-in potential.","Level 2 stays his as his combo out-damages your early trades.","Level 3 is still Pantheon's with passive auto-block and stun pressure.","Level 4 flips to you as the first real ghoul swarm soaks his combo.","Level 6 is his: Grand Starfall lands from 5500 range and slows you.","With first item and Maiden you out-sustain and shove him in.","With 2+ items you out-scale and out-splitpush the falling-off bully."]},
  {"a":"yorick","b":"poppy","win":["Yorick","Skill","Skill","Poppy","Yorick","Yorick","Yorick"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 3-5","text":"Poppy's level 4 is her window: Heroic Charge slams you into a wall for a stun on 14s, and Hammer Shock's zone slows then explodes; Steadfast Presence stops dashes, so it does nothing to you."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Your R Eulogy of the Isles and Maiden overpower Poppy in an extended fight; she has no sustain and can't 1v1 your ghoul wall plus Maiden DPS."},{"when":"1st item","text":"With Tiamat and Maiden you perma-shove Poppy in and win trades; she can only disengage with W, not out-duel your wave and ghouls."},{"when":"Late","text":"Poppy is a peel/anti-dive tank with no splitpush; your Maiden and ghouls take towers and win side-lane duels she can't answer."}],"wants":{"you":["Trade at level 1 with E before her W and E combo is online","Stay clear of walls so Heroic Charge cannot stun you","Shove and out-duel her with Maiden and ghouls after 5"],"foe":["Level 4 E Heroic Charge wall-stun into her Q burst","W Steadfast Presence to slow and ground your escape","Ult your ghouls or you away to peel in a fight"]},"early":"Level 1 is yours: E Mourning Mist plus an auto out-trades Poppy before her W and E combo exists, so poke and take the early edge.","mid":"Respect her level-4 spike, where Heroic Charge into a wall stuns you — play off walls, and never cage next to yourself, since Dark Procession is a wall too. By 5-6 your ghouls and Maiden flip control back.","late":"You dominate late: Poppy is a peel tank with no splitpush answer, so you out-scale into side-lane pressure and take towers with Maiden.","whys":["Level 1 is yours as E and an auto beat Poppy before her combo exists.","Level 2 is even while she builds toward her level-4 spike.","Level 3 stays skill-based just before her W-E stun combo comes online.","Level 4 favors Poppy: E Heroic Charge wall-stun into Q bursts you.","At 6 your R and Maiden overpower her in an extended fight.","With first item and Maiden you shove her in and win trades.","With 2+ items you out-splitpush the peel tank who can't answer Maiden."]},
  {"a":"yorick","b":"quinn","win":["Quinn","Quinn","Quinn","Quinn","Skill","Skill","Yorick"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 3-5","text":"Quinn pokes you off the wave with Blinding Assault (Q) on 11s and her Harrier marks, chunking you before your ghouls stack. Farm with Last Rites, use minions as cover, and never step up for melee CS into a mark proc."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Her Behind Enemy Lines (R) lets her roam or all-in with a speed boost, and she can kite your ghouls in a straight line. Ward river and ping your team when she vanishes. Your R answers waves but not her mobility."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Quinn's lethality spike outpaces your single item; she deletes you if you walk up without ghouls. Play for a full cage-and-Maiden setup rather than solo trades. Shove and look to help other lanes."},{"when":"Late","text":"Behind Enemy Lines is a map tool, not a duel win — she cannot take a tower alone the way Maiden can. Trade objectives, split opposite her, and never chase her into fog where she kites you."}],"wants":{"you":["Ghouls stacked before any trade","Cage her against a wall to remove kite room","Cross-map Maiden pressure while she roams"],"foe":["Poke you down with E and passive before ghouls","Kite backward in open lane","Roam with R to snowball other lanes"]},"early":"Quinn out-ranges you before ghouls form: Blinding Assault blinds from 1025 range on 11s and Vault drops her back at attack range on 12s, denying you melee CS. Play safe, farm with Last Rites, and expect to lose the bully phase.","mid":"Quinn's lethality and R mobility let her pick fights and roam faster than you can react. Your only edge is shoving and matching with Maiden splits. She wins straight duels; you win map trades.","late":"She kites your ghouls in the open, but the side lane is a corridor: cage her against a wall and she has nowhere to fall back. Split opposite her and let Maiden take the towers she leaves.","whys":["Quinn's E poke and passive marks chunk you before ghouls stack, so she owns the early lane.","Quinn out-ranges your melee and steps back after every Vault, keeping you off CS.","Even trades exist only when your ghouls are up, so neither snowballs cleanly here.","Quinn's R roam and speed let her leave and impact the map faster than you can punish.","Ghoul-swarm windows are symmetric mid-game, making full setups roughly coin-flip.","First item is even: her burst is real, but Dark Procession removes her kite room.","Late, Quinn's mobility beats your ghouls anywhere but a walled sidelane, favoring her."]},
  {"a":"yorick","b":"renekton","win":["Renekton","Renekton","Renekton","Renekton","Renekton","Renekton","Yorick"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 3-5","text":"Renekton bullies you with Dice (Q) sustain and dash-slice-dash (E-W-E) burst before your ghouls exist. He can dodge your E and all-in your low-fury windows. Play back, farm with Q, and don't trade until ghouls are up."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Dominus grants bonus health and area damage on 120s at rank 1, and full Fury turns Ruthless Predator into a 1.5s stun that also strips shields. Cage his retreat, never his path in."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Dark Procession blocks movement, so Slice and Dice cannot dash through it — cage the escape route once his Fury bar is empty, then bring the swarm. Shove and roam if he freezes on you."},{"when":"Late","text":"Renekton falls off while you scale; split opposite him and let the Walkers take his side lane. Keep ghouls and Maiden between you, and never take an isolated fight while his Fury is full."}],"wants":{"you":["Wait out his fury bar before trading","Cage him when his dashes are down","Split with Maiden as he falls off late"],"foe":["All-in during your no-ghoul windows","Dash in with E for the stun","Snowball early leads before you scale"]},"early":"Renekton is a lane bully who out-sustains and out-bursts you before ghouls, using Q healing and dash combos to win every early trade. Respect his fury windows, farm safely with Q, and never fight at low ghoul count. He wins the opening phase decisively.","mid":"He still holds the tempo edge, but Dark Procession blocks movement — Slice and Dice does not dash through it. Bait an empty Fury bar, cage the escape, then swarm him with the ghouls.","late":"Renekton fades as you hit full ghoul-and-Maiden scaling, but a fed one stays lethal in isolation. Split opposite him, force side-lane pressure, and only fight with your swarm assembled and his Fury bar empty.","whys":["Renekton's Q sustain and dash burst crush your no-ghoul early, giving him the lane.","His dash-slice-dash combo out-trades you before ghouls form, so he bullies freely.","Even windows appear only when his fury is empty and your ghouls are stacked.","Levels 4-5 stay his: Slice and Dice is back every 13s at rank 3.","Ghoul-swarm setups roughly balance the mid-game when he lacks dash cooldowns.","Renekton's item and mobility let him ignore your cage on his terms.","Two-plus items are yours: split away and Maiden takes towers he must answer."]},
  {"a":"yorick","b":"riven","win":["Skill","Riven","Riven","Riven","Riven","Riven","Yorick"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 3-5","text":"Broken Wings is a 13s three-part combo ending in a knockback, and Ki Burst stuns every 11s at rank 1, so she all-ins before ghouls exist. Dark Procession blocks movement, so Valor cannot dash it. Farm with Last Rites, never into full charges."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Blade of the Exile is 120s at rank 1: bonus damage, extra range, and one Wind Slash projectile. Do not step up while Ki Burst and Valor are both up — wait until she spends them."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Her item spike is real, but Valor is a 250-range step and Dark Procession blocks movement — cage the escape once her charges are spent, then swarm. Shove and roam rather than duel."},{"when":"Late","text":"Riven stays a lethal duelist, but she has to be present to duel — Maiden and the Walkers take a tower whether you are there or not. Split opposite her, avoid open skirmishes, and force her to fight into the cage."}],"wants":{"you":["Trade only when her Q and dash are spent","Cage her against a wall to deny dashes","Split with Maiden while dodging duels"],"foe":["All-in during your no-ghoul windows","Animation-cancel her Broken Wings burst","Snowball early kills into a lead"]},"early":"Riven is a hard lane bully: Broken Wings on 13s and Ki Burst on 11s let her all-in before ghouls form. Dark Procession blocks movement, so Valor does not dash through it. Farm with Last Rites and trade only once her charges and shield are down.","mid":"Riven holds tempo through this phase; she picks fights and escapes the swarm. Bait Broken Wings' three casts and Valor's shield, then cage the retreat — the wall blocks her step forward.","late":"Riven remains a mobile duelist, but she has to show up to duel, and you do not. Split opposite her with Maiden, take towers while she chases, and fight only inside your own cage.","whys":["Riven's Q-dash-stun all-in crushes your no-ghoul early, handing her the lane.","Her mobility and animation-cancel burst out-trade you before ghouls stack.","Even windows exist only when her Q charges and shield are fully spent.","Levels 4-5 are hers: Ki Burst stuns every 9s and Valor shields.","Level 6 is hers: Blade of the Exile adds range and one Wind Slash.","First item is hers, but the cage blocks Valor — she cannot dash it.","Late, Riven's dashes kite your ghouls in the open, favoring her outside your cage."]},
  {"a":"yorick","b":"rumble","win":["Skill","Rumble","Rumble","Skill","Skill","Rumble","Rumble"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 3-5","text":"Rumble's Flamespitter (Q) and Electro Harpoon (E) shred you and your ghouls from range before you can commit. Danger-Zone Q melts your swarm and you at once. Last Rites is melee — last-hit from outside his 600-range cone."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"The Equalizer (R) zones you off the wave and can burn you inside your own Dark Procession. It is 130s at rank 1 — cage him only after it is spent, and use Eulogy to hold a sidelane he can't zone."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Rumble spikes hard on his first AP item, out-poking and out-DPSing your ghouls in extended fights. Force him to burn heat, then all-in during his overheat lockout. Your E slow helps pin him."},{"when":"Late","text":"You out-scale Rumble's teamfight ceiling in the sidelane, where his R matters less and your Maiden pressures relentlessly. Split away from his R zones and swarm him one-on-one. Avoid grouped fights where his ult shines."}],"wants":{"you":["All-in during his overheat lockout","Cage and swarm him with R down","Split with Maiden away from his R"],"foe":["Poke you and ghouls with heated Q","Zone your cage and wave with R","Spike on first AP item to out-DPS"]},"early":"Rumble out-pokes you and the pack with Danger-Zone Flamespitter, shredding Mist Walkers before you commit. Last Rites is melee, so last-hit from outside his 600 cone and wait for Overheat. He controls the opening lane.","mid":"Rumble's R zoning and AP spike let him deny your cage and out-DPS extended trades. Bait his heat, then all-in during his overheat lockout with ghouls up. Roughly even once you punish his cooldowns.","late":"You out-scale Rumble in the sidelane where his ultimate matters less and Maiden pressures constantly. Split away from his R zones, swarm him solo, and avoid grouped fights. Your split ceiling beats his.","whys":["Rumble's heated Q shreds you and your ghouls before you commit, owning the early.","His ranged poke out-trades your melee swarm through the laning phase.","Even trades open only during his overheat lockout with ghouls stacked.","Yorick's cage-and-swarm lands cleanly when Rumble's R is on cooldown, favoring you.","Rumble's first AP item spike out-DPSes your ghouls in extended fights.","Your Maiden split pressures harder than Rumble can answer alone, favoring you.","Late, your sidelane ceiling beats Rumble's ult-reliant teamfight kit one-on-one."]},
  {"a":"yorick","b":"ryze","win":["Yorick","Skill","Skill","Skill","Skill","Ryze","Yorick"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 3-5","text":"Ryze is immobile and mana-starved, and Last Rites out-sustains his chip. Mourning Mist (E, 700) outranges Rune Prison and Spell Flux at 615 — mark from outside, then wall the retreat."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Ryze has no combat ult and stays vulnerable to your cage-and-swarm at 6. Keep pressuring with ghouls and E marks while he's mana-starved. This is your strongest window to snowball."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Ryze's first item mana spike lets him root-combo your ghouls and poke you down from range. Watch his root chain and W snare into cage. The lane tips toward even as he comes online."},{"when":"Late","text":"Ryze scales into a burst mage who deletes your ghouls and roams with his R teleport, out-pacing your split. Force sidelane duels where his teamfight kit is wasted, but respect his root-burst combo. He edges you in the open."}],"wants":{"you":["All-in early while he's mana-starved","Cage and swarm before he gets items","E-mark and pressure his low mobility"],"foe":["Stack items and mana to out-poke you","Root-chain your ghouls from range","Roam with R teleport to out-pace splits"]},"early":"Ryze is immobile and mana-starved early, so your ghouls, Q, and E marks out-trade his weak root poke. Step up, cage, and swarm to snowball before he stacks items. This is a clear early advantage for you.","mid":"Once Ryze hits his mana item, his root chains and range let him contest your swarm and poke you down. Keep punishing his low mobility but respect the snare-into-combo. The lane levels off here.","late":"Ryze scales into a burst-and-root mage who clears your ghouls and roams with R, out-pacing your split. Force sidelane duels where his teamfight strength is wasted, and dodge his root chain. He edges the open map.","whys":["Ryze is immobile and mana-starved early, so your ghouls and E-mark out-trade him.","Yorick's cage all-in punishes Ryze's short root range before he stacks items.","Dark Procession returns every 20s at rank 1 — cage him and the swarm wins, else even.","Ryze's first mana item lets his root-chain contest your ghouls, leveling the lane.","Eulogy of the Isles makes it 2v1, but Realm Warp lets him reposition away — even at six.","Ryze's first mana item lets Overload chains clear ghouls faster than you refill them.","Late, Maiden plus a full ghoul army makes your side lane unanswerable by Ryze alone."]},
  {"a":"yorick","b":"sejuani","win":["Yorick","Yorick","Yorick","Yorick","Skill","Yorick","Yorick"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 3-5","text":"Sejuani is tanky and low-damage, but Fury of the North's Frost Armor gives armour, MR and slow immunity — Mourning Mist's slow does nothing until it breaks. Its mark and armour shred still land, so lead with it and swarm."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Glacial Prison is 120s at rank 1 and sets up a gank, but she lacks the solo burst if you swarm back. Save Dark Procession for Arctic Assault — walling her 650-range charge strands her in the pack."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Sejuani builds tanky and won't out-damage you; you build a lead through CS and ghoul pressure. Keep marking her with E to let ghouls chip her armor. The lane stays roughly balanced but tilts your way."},{"when":"Late","text":"You out-scale her in the sidelane, where her tank kit offers little solo threat and your Maiden shoves relentlessly. Split away from her team, swarm her one-on-one, and dodge her R engage. Your split ceiling wins."}],"wants":{"you":["Build a CS lead with ghoul pressure","Split with Maiden away from her team","Swarm her tanky solo profile late"],"foe":["Sustain through poke with Frost Armor","Set up ganks with R stun","Peel and engage in grouped fights"]},"early":"Sejuani is a tanky, low-damage laner who can't burst you, and you can't quickly kill through her Frost Armor sustain, making the early phase an even farm race. Trade with E marks when her passive is down and build a CS edge. Neither snowballs cleanly.","mid":"Sejuani's R stun enables ganks but she lacks solo kill threat if you cage and swarm. You slowly build a lead through ghoul pressure and marks. The lane stays balanced but leans your direction.","late":"You out-scale Sejuani in the sidelane, where her tank kit offers no solo threat and Maiden shoves hard. Split away from her team, swarm her one-on-one, and dodge her R engage. Your split ceiling clearly wins.","whys":["Arctic Assault is 18s at rank 1 — she has one engage and no way to contest your graves.","Your first Mist Walkers arrive before she can stack Frost for Permafrost.","Dark Procession cuts off Arctic Assault, her only gap-closer, on an 18s cooldown.","Glacial Prison sets up ganks but gives her no solo kill on you.","Sejuani's tank build won't out-damage you, but she survives your pressure, staying even.","Yorick out-scales her weak solo profile with Maiden splits, favoring you late-lane.","Late, Yorick's split ceiling and one-on-one swarm beat Sejuani's tank kit, favoring you."]},
  {"a":"yorick","b":"sett","win":["Yorick","Sett","Sett","Sett","Sett","Sett","Yorick"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 3-5","text":"Sett trades evenly early; his passive punch and Haymaker (W) shield punish you if you dump ghouls carelessly. Trade with E-mark and Q, keep ghouls chipping, and don't feed his W with big hits. A close, skill-based opening."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Sett's Facebreaker (E) grab and R suppression let him all-in you at 6, and his W shield eats your ghoul burst. Save W-cage for his engage and E to slow his exit. He holds the kill threat this level."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Sett's item spike and shield uptime tilt short trades his way; don't brawl into a full grit bar. Bait his W, then swarm during the cooldown. The lane is close but he edges skirmishes here."},{"when":"Late","text":"You out-scale Sett in the sidelane, where his engage kit is wasted and your Maiden shoves relentlessly. Split away from his team, swarm him one-on-one when his W is down, and dodge his E-R chain. Your split ceiling wins."}],"wants":{"you":["Chip his shield with ghouls, not big hits","Split with Maiden away from his team","Swarm him late when W is on cooldown"],"foe":["Punish careless ghoul dumps with W shield","All-in with E grab and R at 6","Win short trades on his grit spike"]},"early":"Sett trades on roughly even terms early; his passive and W shield punish careless ghoul dumps while your E-mark and Q chip him down. Keep ghouls poking without feeding his Haymaker, and the opening stays a close skill match. Neither dominates.","mid":"Sett's E grab, R suppression, and shield uptime give him the kill threat around 6 and on his item spike. Bait his W, then swarm during the cooldown. He edges the short-trade skirmishes this phase.","late":"You out-scale Sett in the sidelane, where his engage kit is wasted and Maiden shoves hard. Split away from his team, swarm him solo when his W is down, and dodge his E-R chain. Your split ceiling clearly wins.","whys":["Mourning Mist reaches 700 and marks him for your pack — level 1 is yours.","Sett's grit spike and shield let him win the short trades he seeks around level 2-3.","Every ghoul hit he takes feeds Grit — his Haymaker only grows through level 3.","Facebreaker into a full-Grit Haymaker beats your swarm until Eulogy is online.","The Show Stopper lands at 6 on 120s and drags you out of your own pack.","His first item plus Grit uptime keeps short trades his until your second.","Late, Yorick's split ceiling and solo swarm beat Sett's wasted engage, favoring you."]},
  {"a":"yorick","b":"shen","win":["Skill","Shen","Shen","Shen","Shen","Shen","Yorick"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 3-5","text":"Ki Barrier procs after Shen casts a spell, not off autos, so it is up in every trade you take. Spirit's Refuge is 16s at rank 1 and blocks attacks near his blade — walk the pack out of that zone before you commit."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Shen's R Stand United is a global that pulls him out of your lane to save teammates; punish the tempo by shoving the wave with ghouls and R Eulogy the moment he channels or leaves, taking plates or a dive."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Shen's first tank item plus Twilight Assault's max-health damage out-lasts a ghoul pile; hold the all-in until Spirit's Refuge is on its 16 seconds."},{"when":"Late","text":"Shen wants to teamfight and roam via R, but you sidelane unkillable with Maiden and W Dark Procession cage; force him to answer your split or lose towers."}],"wants":{"you":["E Mourning Mist to close and slow, never wasting it","permanent ghoul pressure to zone his CS and shield procs","punishing his R absences to take plates and prio"],"foe":["proc Ki Barrier off every spell cast to shield the trade","land taunt E Shadow Dash to survive your ghoul pile","use global R to gain map value away from your lane"]},"early":"You start ahead: E Mourning Mist gives vision, a slow, and bonus damage, and your ghouls swarm Shen before his passive shield can stabilize, so every level 1-2 poke and trade favors you.","mid":"From 3 onward Shadow Dash answers your all-in every 18s, so hold the pattern until it is spent. When Stand United pulls him out of lane, shove with the pack and take plates.","late":"With first item and Maiden you're an unkillable split-pusher; Shen's teamfight-and-roam identity can't stop your sidelane, so you bleed his towers while he's forced to respond.","whys":["You win level 1 because E Mourning Mist and early ghouls out-trade Shen's weak lane sustain.","Ki Barrier refreshes off every spell, so his second-level shield outlasts your chip.","Shadow Dash arrives at 3 on an 18s cooldown and taunts you out of your own swarm.","You favor levels 4-5 because Q Last Rites plus a full ghoul pack overwhelms his shield-and-taunt kit.","Stand United is global, so he trades your level-6 spike for a kill in another lane.","His first tank item plus Ki Barrier absorbs more than a ghoul pile puts out.","You win 2+ items because your unkillable split beats Shen's roam-reliant teamfight identity."]},
  {"a":"yorick","b":"singed","win":["Yorick","Yorick","Skill","Singed","Singed","Singed","Yorick"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 3-5","text":"Once Singed hits 3 his W Mega Adhesive plus Q Poison Trail lets him proxy and fling; if you chase him into his goo you eat a flip into E Fling and turret, so hold ghouls and only commit with E Mourning Mist landed."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Your R Eulogy of the Isles and Maiden let you crash waves and take plates faster than Singed can proxy, flipping tempo back to you as he can't duel your ghoul pile."},{"when":"1st item","text":"With Bramble/Sunderer and Maiden you shove and deny his proxy; Singed's Rylai's-slow poke can't kill you through ghoul sustain, so you snowball tower plates."},{"when":"Late","text":"Late, Maiden and a full ghoul pack take towers faster than Singed proxies them back. Never chase him through Poison Trail — take the objective he walked away from and let him run."}],"wants":{"you":["land E Mourning Mist before ever chasing him","use ghouls and Maiden to out-shove his proxy","take plates while he's proxying instead of chasing"],"foe":["W Mega Adhesive then E Fling you under his turret","proxy waves to deny your ghoul-stacked pushes","use flip disruption to peel and flank in fights"]},"early":"You edge the very early game: E Mourning Mist slows him and your ghouls contest CS before Singed has W Mega Adhesive online, so a clean level 1-2 trade favors you.","mid":"Levels 2-3 even out as his Q Poison Trail and proxy playstyle come online, then he tilts ahead at 4-5 when W plus E Fling can flip your chase into a turret death; don't dive his goo.","late":"His six and first item are his window — Insanity Potion's Grievous Wounds halves Last Rites for its full 100 seconds. Past two items, Maiden and the pack out-take towers faster than he can proxy them back.","whys":["You win level 1 because E Mourning Mist and ghoul CS pressure beat pre-W Singed.","Fling is only 125 range, so he has to walk into your first Mist Walker.","Level 3 is even because his W Mega Adhesive comes online to punish over-chasing.","Singed favors levels 4-5 as W into E Fling can flip your dive into his turret.","Insanity Potion makes Poison Trail apply Grievous Wounds, halving Last Rites.","You win first item as ghoul sustain denies his poke and you snowball plates.","Two items in, Maiden and a full pack take towers faster than he can proxy them back."]},
  {"a":"yorick","b":"sion","win":["Yorick","Sion","Sion","Sion","Skill","Sion","Yorick"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 3-5","text":"At 3 Sion's Q Decimating Smash charge plus E Roar of the Slayer poke starts to trade back; a fully-charged Q knock-up onto your ghoul pile can turn a fight, so bait it out with E Mourning Mist range before committing."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Your R Eulogy and Maiden let you crash and take plates while Sion is stuck farming; his R Unstoppable Onslaught is a roam/engage tool, not a duel button, so lane tempo swings to you."},{"when":"1st item","text":"With Sunderer and Maiden your all-in beats his shield-W passive; Sion can't out-DPS a Maiden pile once his Q is on cooldown, so you win extended trades."},{"when":"Late","text":"Late, Maiden and a full pack take towers faster than Sion answers alone. He is an engage tank, not a duelist — make him choose between your split and the fight he wants."}],"wants":{"you":["poke with E Mourning Mist outside his Q charge range","all-in with ghouls when his Q Decimating Smash is down","take plates while he's stuck farming, not dueling"],"foe":["land a charged Q knock-up into E for a big trade","use W Soul Furnace shield to tank your ghoul burst","flank with R Unstoppable Onslaught to disrupt fights"]},"early":"You start ahead: E Mourning Mist out-ranges his early poke and your ghouls contest CS before Sion's Q Decimating Smash is a threat, so level 1-2 trades favor you.","mid":"Levels 2-3 even out once his Q charge and E Roar poke come online; at 4-5 a fully-charged Q knock-up into your stack can swing a trade his way, so respect the charge and only commit with E landed.","late":"You take tempo back at 6 and first item as Maiden shoves and takes plates while he farms, but by 2+ items Sion's tank frontline, W shield, and R flank engage outvalue your straight split.","whys":["You win level 1 because E Mourning Mist and ghoul CS pressure beat Sion's short early range.","A fully charged Decimating Smash knocks up on a 10s cooldown — level 2 is his.","Level 3 is even with E Roar of the Slayer poke and W shield stabilizing him.","Sion favors levels 4-5 because a charged Q knock-up into your pile wins the big trade.","Eulogy is 160s and Unstoppable Onslaught 140s — both ults are map tools.","You win first item as a Maiden pile out-DPSes his shield once Q is on cooldown.","Two items in, Maiden and the pack take towers he must leave a fight to defend."]},
  {"a":"yorick","b":"swain","win":["Skill","Swain","Swain","Skill","Skill","Swain","Yorick"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 3-5","text":"Vision of Empire and Death's Hand chunk you before you close, and every W that lands hands him a Soul Fragment. Nevermove roots on its return trip, not on the way out — walk through the outgoing wave and keep moving."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"His R Demonic Ascension heals him massively in extended fights; do not all-in through his ult uptime, and instead shove with ghouls and R Eulogy to deny CS rather than duel."},{"when":"1st item","text":"With Rylai's/Liandry's Swain's E-root into R sustain is a full combo that out-heals your ghoul DPS in a straight duel; pick your engage only when his E is on cooldown."},{"when":"Late","text":"Late Swain is a drain-tank frontliner whose R heal and E root anchor teamfights; your split-push is the win condition, so avoid his fights and take towers instead of contesting him."}],"wants":{"you":["body-block E Nevermove with ghouls and minions","engage only when his E root is down","split and take towers rather than duel his R heal"],"foe":["poke you down with Q Death's Hand and W Vision of Empire","land E Nevermove root to lock in a full combo","sustain through your ghouls with R Demonic Ascension"]},"early":"Swain starts ahead: his Q Death's Hand and W Vision of Empire out-range your E Mourning Mist, so he pokes you off CS before your ghouls can pressure him at all in levels 1-2.","mid":"Level 3 is even once your ghoul pack lets you contest, and 4-5 stay even if you body-block his E Nevermove and refuse to walk into his poke; the lane hinges on dodging that root.","late":"He tilts back ahead at 6 with R Demonic Ascension healing through your all-in, and by 2+ items his drain-tank frontline out-sustains any duel, so your answer is to split and take towers, not fight him.","whys":["Death's Hand out-ranges you at 750, but level 1 he has one spell and no root.","Swain wins level 2 as W Vision of Empire adds zone-poke you can't answer.","Level 3 is even once your ghoul pack lets you contest CS and trades.","Levels 4-5 are even if you body-block E Nevermove and dodge his poke.","Demonic Ascension is 120s and drains — Grievous Wounds is what makes six even.","Swain wins first item as E-root into R is a full combo that out-sustains you.","Two items in, Maiden and the pack take towers he cannot leave a fight to hold."]},
  {"a":"yorick","b":"sylas","win":["Skill","Sylas","Sylas","Sylas","Sylas","Sylas","Yorick"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 3-5","text":"Sylas wants to Q Chain Lash then E Abscond/Abduct in for burst, but your ghoul pile plus E Mourning Mist slow punishes him hard on the way out; force him to trade into your stack and he loses the exchange."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"His R Hijack steals your ultimate, but Eulogy of the Isles' Maiden isn't a burst tool he can turn against you like a real teamfight ult, so his ult value is low here while your wave crash and plates keep pressuring."},{"when":"1st item","text":"With Sunderer and Maiden you out-sustain his W Kingslayer heal and out-DPS his combo in extended fights; once his E dash is down he can't escape your ghouls."},{"when":"Late","text":"Late Sylas is a roaming assassin/skirmisher, but you sidelane unkillable with Maiden and W Dark Procession; he can't 1v1 your split and gains little from hijacking your R."}],"wants":{"you":["land E Mourning Mist to slow his E escape","make him trade into your full ghoul pile","punish his E dash cooldown for a clean all-in"],"foe":["burst with Q Chain Lash into E Abscond then out","heal back with W Kingslayer in extended trades","roam and skirmish rather than 1v1 your split"]},"early":"You start ahead: E Mourning Mist gives a slow and bonus damage while your ghouls contest CS, and Sylas's early poke can't out-trade your stack before his E dash is up in levels 1-2.","mid":"Level 2-3 even out as his Q Chain Lash and W Kingslayer heal come online, but from 4-5 onward your ghoul pile plus E slow punish every Q-E commit, tilting the lane back to you.","late":"You stay ahead through 6 and items: his R Hijack gets little from your Maiden-summon ult, and your Sunderer-Maiden all-in out-sustains W and out-DPSes his combo, leaving you the unkillable split threat.","whys":["Mourning Mist reaches 700 to his 775 Chain Lash — level 1 trades cut both ways.","Kingslayer heals him off champions on a 12s cooldown you cannot match yet.","Abscond in, Abduct back out on 13s — he leaves your pack whenever he likes.","Chain Lash drops to 7s by rank 4 and out-ranges Mourning Mist by 75 units.","Hijack is 80s at rank 1 and steals Eulogy — he gets a Maiden of his own.","His first AP item plus Kingslayer's heal out-lasts what a ghoul pile puts out.","You win 2+ items since your unkillable split beats his skirmish-roam identity."]},
  {"a":"yorick","b":"tahmkench","win":["Skill","Yorick","Yorick","Skill","Skill","Yorick","Yorick"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 3-5","text":"Tongue Lash needs three An Acquired Taste stacks to stun, and three stacks is also what lets him Devour you. Trade through Mist Walkers and Mourning Mist instead of eating repeated 900-range Qs, and he gets neither."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Devour (R) is the pick tool; Abyssal Dive (W) is a separate 21s knock-up escape. Your pack out-damages Thick Skin's grey-health regen — crash the wave and take plates while he farms."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Thick Skin banks a share of everything you deal and cashes it as a shield on a 3s cooldown — bring Grievous Wounds, then commit with Mourning Mist landed."},{"when":"Late","text":"Late Tahm is a peel/save support-tank whose R rescues carries, but you split unkillable with Maiden and W Dark Procession; he can't 1v1 you and gains little standing in your sidelane."}],"wants":{"you":["deny his passive stacks so Q Tongue Lash can't stun","all-in with ghouls plus E before he regens grey health","take plates while he farms defensively"],"foe":["stack Acquired Taste for a Q Tongue Lash stun","bank grey health with Thick Skin (E)","save teammates with R Devour in fights"]},"early":"Level 1 is even as Tahm's Q Tongue Lash and W lane presence match your opener, but you don't yet have the ghoul pack to punish, so it's a wash on the first trade.","mid":"From 2 onward you take over: Mist Walkers plus Mourning Mist out-trade him if you deny An Acquired Taste stacks — three of them is a stun and a Devour. Thick Skin regens the rest, so bring Grievous Wounds.","late":"You stay ahead through 6 and items as Sunderer and Maiden shred his tanky sustain and your unkillable split beats a Tahm who's built to peel and save rather than 1v1 your sidelane.","whys":["Level 1 is even as Tahm's Q and W lane presence match your opener before your ghouls stack.","You win level 2 because your ghoul pack plus E out-trade him and deny his passive stacks.","Thick Skin, not his W, banks grey health — it cashes as a shield on 3s.","You win levels 4-5 because your ghoul pile plus E slow out-DPS his sustain.","You win level 6 by out-shoving 1v1 and taking plates while he can only farm.","You win first item as Sunderer and Maiden shred through his grey-health sustain.","You win 2+ items since your unkillable split beats his peel-and-save tank identity."]},
  {"a":"yorick","b":"teemo","win":["Teemo","Teemo","Teemo","Skill","Teemo","Skill","Teemo"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 3-5","text":"Teemo's Q Blinding Dart disables your auto-attacks, and his passive Guerrilla Warfare stealth plus E Toxic Shot poke chunks you as you walk up; hold minions between you and only close behind a landed E Mourning Mist and full ghoul pack."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Noxious Trap reaches 600 at rank 1 and bounces further when thrown onto another mushroom, so a shroom line covers more ground than it looks. Clear them with Mist Walkers, not your face, and stay out of fog."},{"when":"1st item","text":"With Blinding Dart plus Liandry's/Nashor's poke Teemo kites your ghouls and blinds your DPS window; you need Merc treads and to force him under tower where ghouls can trade the Q blind."},{"when":"Late","text":"Late Teemo shroom-walls the map and pokes from stealth; your split still threatens towers, but his blind and shroom zoning slow every push and let him escape your all-ins."}],"wants":{"you":["close only behind a landed E Mourning Mist","use minions to block his Q Blinding Dart and E poke","clear shrooms with ghouls instead of tanking them"],"foe":["Q Blinding Dart to disable your autos in every trade","poke you down with E Toxic Shot and stealth resets","shroom-wall your ghoul paths with R Noxious Trap"]},"early":"Teemo starts ahead: his Q Blinding Dart shuts off your autos and E Toxic Shot plus stealth poke chunks you before you ever reach him, so levels 1-2 are a losing walk-up.","mid":"Level 3 evens out once your ghoul pack lets you trade even through a blind, but at 4-5 his sustained Q-and-E poke tilts back to him unless you land E Mourning Mist to force the gap closed.","late":"Level 6 and items favor Teemo as R Noxious Trap shrooms zone your paths and his blind denies your DPS; your split still pressures towers, but expect slow, shroom-walled pushes rather than clean kills.","whys":["Teemo wins level 1 because Q Blinding Dart disables your autos in the opening trade.","Teemo wins level 2 as E Toxic Shot and stealth poke chunk you on every walk-up.","Level 3 is even once your ghoul pack lets you trade through the blind.","Teemo favors levels 4-5 because his sustained Q-and-E poke out-damages your approach.","Noxious Trap arrives at 6 and shrooms every path your pack has to walk.","Teemo wins first item as Blinding Dart plus poke items kite your ghoul DPS.","Teemo wins 2+ items because R shroom zoning walls your split and slows every push."]},
  {"a":"yorick","b":"trundle","win":["Trundle","Trundle","Trundle","Trundle","Trundle","Trundle","Yorick"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 3-5","text":"Trundle's spike, not yours: Chomp (Q, 3.5s) saps your AD, and King's Tribute heals him whenever a unit dies near him — your own Mist Walkers included. Frozen Domain (W, 750 range) amplifies all his healing while he stands on it. Never brawl on the zone; Mourning Mist and reset."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Trundle's Subjugate (R) drains a huge chunk of your max health and resistances, deleting your bruiser stats in a fight. Play the map with your Eulogy of the Isles (R) Maiden pushing a side lane instead of standing to trade his ultimate."},{"when":"1st item","text":"This is where you flip it: your ghouls plus Maiden overwhelm Trundle's single-target sustain, and Bramble Vest / grievous wounds guts his Chomp and pillar healing. Group your Shepherd of Souls minions and shove him off the wave."},{"when":"Late","text":"Yorick dominates the side-lane sim: Maiden plus a full ghoul cage means Trundle can't 1v1 your split and can't leave without conceding a tower. Force him to answer you while your team takes objectives 4v4."}],"wants":{"you":["Reach items and Maiden to out-DPS his sustain","Grievous wounds (Bramble/Thornmail) to cut Chomp and Domain healing","Side-lane sims where ghouls swarm his single target"],"foe":["Early all-ins on his Frozen Domain (W) speed zone","Chomp (Q) AD-steal trades to snowball stats","Subjugate (R) to melt your bruiser HP and resistances in a fight"]},"early":"Trundle wins levels 1-2 flat out: Chomp (Q) saps your AD and heals him, so any auto-trade leaves you weaker and him fuller. Last Rites is a melee auto-reset that heals you — use it on the wave, keep Mist Walkers between you, and never stand on Frozen Domain (W).","mid":"Levels 3-6 stay Trundle-favoured: Frozen Domain (W) lets him chase and amplifies his healing, and Subjugate at 6 on 120s strips a share of your health and both resistances. Pillar of Ice (E, 21s, 1000 range) is what splits you from your pack — hold Dark Procession for after it, and clear waves rather than duel.","late":"Once you hit your first item and Maiden, the matchup flips hard to Yorick: your ghoul swarm plus Eulogy Maiden out-damages his single-target healing, and grievous wounds neutralizes his Chomp and pillar. Split-push relentlessly and make Trundle choose between your tower and the map.","whys":["Trundle's Chomp (Q) steals your AD and heals every trade, owning level 1.","At 2 his sustain and Frozen Domain (W) keep him ahead in extended pokes.","Level 3 his full early kit out-sustains your Q Last Rites brawls.","Levels 4-5 his Chomp trades and Domain speed let him dictate every fight.","At 6 Subjugate (R) strips your HP and resistances, hard-favouring Trundle.","First item plus Maiden lets your ghoul swarm finally out-DPS his sustain.","With 2+ items Yorick's split-push and grievous wounds bury his single-target healing."]},
  {"a":"yorick","b":"tryndamere","win":["Skill","Yorick","Yorick","Skill","Skill","Yorick","Yorick"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 3-5","text":"Even window: Tryndamere's Spinning Slash (E) gap-close and Mocking Shout (W) slow let him stick, but your Mourning Mist (E) marks him for a guaranteed ghoul dash and slow so you can peel back. Trade only when your W Dark Procession cage is up to wall his escape."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Tryndamere spikes with Undying Rage (R): 5 seconds unkillable on a 120/100/80s cooldown, so a kill you set up he survives and leaves on Spinning Slash (E). Never spend your full combo through his ult; bait it, then re-engage inside those 100 seconds."},{"when":"1st item","text":"His crit scaling starts to bite and Fury-fueled autos shred you, but your ghoul wall plus Maiden means he can't cleanly all-in without eating a cage. Build early armor (Bramble) so his crits do less and your sustain holds."},{"when":"Late","text":"Split-push race: Tryndamere is one of the best splitters in the game with R + E to escape ganks, so you can't out-roam him. Match him lane-for-lane with Maiden and ghouls, but respect that his R makes him near-impossible to punish 1v1."}],"wants":{"you":["Mourning Mist (E) marks to slow and kite his engage","W Dark Procession cage to wall his Spinning Slash escape","Armor items to blunt his Fury crits in extended trades"],"foe":["Fury-stacked crit autos to burst you in melee","Undying Rage (R) to negate your kill pressure and disengage","Spinning Slash (E) mobility to dodge ganks and win the split race"]},"early":"Tryndamere owns levels 1-2: his passive Fury builds crit chance fast and his autos plus Bloodlust healing beat your early Q Last Rites trades. Don't try to win the auto-war; farm safely with ghoul soak from Shepherd of Souls and poke with E Mourning Mist when he goes for CS.","mid":"Levels 3-6 settle into a skill window where your Mourning Mist mark and W cage can peel his Spinning Slash, but at 6 his Undying Rage flips it back: he survives everything for 5 seconds. Play for CS and prio rather than kills, since his R denies your all-in and lets him escape.","late":"Tryndamere pulls ahead again with crit items and R as the premier split-pusher; his E mobility dodges the ganks that would punish him. You can't kill him solo, so mirror his split with Maiden and ghouls, build armor to survive crits, and let your team leverage the 4v4 while he's shoved out.","whys":["Level 1 hinges on spacing: his Bloodlust heal versus your Q Last Rites.","At 2 your E mark plus first ghouls out-trade his raw autos.","Level 3 evens out as your Mourning Mist (E) mark and cage let you peel.","Levels 4-5 stay even with cage timing offsetting his Spinning Slash aggression.","At 6 skill holds briefly, but expect Undying Rage (R) to deny kills.","Trinity Force plus Maiden lets you win the first-item side lane.","Two items in, Maiden plus ghouls out-siege him — cage his Spinning Slash."]},
  {"a":"yorick","b":"urgot","win":["Skill","Skill","Skill","Urgot","Urgot","Yorick","Yorick"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 3-5","text":"Urgot's Purge (W) shreds you if you stand in it, and his Corrosive Charge (Q) plus shotgun-knee autos out-poke you at melee range once he hits 3-4. Respect his Q slow zone and only step up behind ghouls; don't feed his W by trading into it."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Fear the Fear Beyond Death (R): fired from 2500 range on a 100/85/70s cooldown, it impales you and, below the execute threshold, drags you in for a guaranteed kill. Keep your HP above that line, and hold Dark Procession (W) to wall him off after he flips you."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Yorick takes over here: your ghoul swarm and Maiden out-damage Urgot's clunky leg rotation, and he has no way to clear a full ghoul cage. Shove the wave and force him under tower where his Q/W poke matters less."},{"when":"Late","text":"Yorick wins the split hands-down: Urgot is immobile and Maiden plus ghouls out-DPS him in any sidelane sim. He can't leave without losing his tower to your push, so drag him around the map and let your team play 4v4."}],"wants":{"you":["First item plus Maiden to out-DPS his leg rotation","Ghoul cage (W Dark Procession) to trap his immobile frame","Sidelane sims where he can't clear your swarm or escape"],"foe":["Corrosive Charge (Q) zone and Purge (W) to out-poke at melee","Fear Beyond Death (R) execute-flip once you drop low","Legs-and-shotgun DPS to win short early trades"]},"early":"Levels 1-3 are a skill window: Urgot's Corrosive Charge (Q) and shotgun-knee autos out-range your melee, but you can farm safely with Q Last Rites and soak his poke on ghouls from Shepherd of Souls. Don't stand in his Q slow, and mark him with Mourning Mist (E) only to disengage cleanly.","mid":"Levels 4-6 tip to Urgot: he activates his legs for constant shotgun DPS and his Purge (W) shreds you in extended trades, then his ult at 6 threatens an execute-flip whenever you dip low. Stay above his R threshold, farm patiently, and don't commit to a brawl you can't finish before his legs and W win it.","late":"From your first item on, Yorick flips it decisively: ghouls plus Maiden out-DPS Urgot's slow leg rotation and his immobility makes him a free split-push target. Cage him with W, swarm him with ghouls, and make his lack of escape a liability while you pressure sidelanes.","whys":["Level 1 is even; his poke exists but neither champ commits.","At 2 it stays skill as you farm safely behind ghoul soak.","Level 3 remains even with careful spacing around his Q zone.","Levels 4-5 favour Urgot once his legs and Purge (W) out-DPS you.","At 6 Fear Beyond Death (R) threatens an execute-flip, keeping Urgot ahead.","First item plus Maiden lets your ghoul swarm out-damage his rotation.","Late, Yorick's split and cage bury the immobile Urgot."]},
  {"a":"yorick","b":"vayne","win":["Vayne","Vayne","Vayne","Skill","Vayne","Vayne","Vayne"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 3-5","text":"Even-ish window but stay wary: Vayne's Tumble (Q) resets her spacing and Silver Bolts (W) true-damage stacks punish you for chasing. Use Mourning Mist (E) to slow her Tumble and force ghoul dashes onto her, and hold W Dark Procession to wall her Condemn escape."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Final Hour (R) gives Vayne invisibility on Tumble, extra AD, and faster stacking; she'll kite your whole combo and delete you if you overextend. Don't dive her when her ult is up; use your Eulogy Maiden to zone and split rather than commit to a kill."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Vayne's item spike is brutal top: Blade of the Ruined King plus Silver Bolts melts even your bruiser HP, and Condemn (E) stuns you into a wall to reset. Rush Bramble Vest and armor, and never let her back you into terrain."},{"when":"Late","text":"Vayne is a hypercarry that out-scales your DPS if she gets going, but she's squishy and immobile without Tumble on cooldown. Split with Maiden and ghouls to deny her farm, and make your team collapse on her since a caged Vayne dies fast."}],"wants":{"you":["Mourning Mist (E) slow to close on her and stop Tumble kiting","W Dark Procession cage to wall her Condemn (E) reset","Armor rush (Bramble) to survive Silver Bolts true damage"],"foe":["Tumble (Q) spacing to kite your ghouls and melee range","Silver Bolts (W) true damage to melt your bruiser HP","Final Hour (R) invisibility and Condemn (E) stun to reset every trade"]},"early":"Vayne owns levels 1-2: her Tumble (Q) auto-resets and Silver Bolts (W) true damage punish any all-in, and her range means she pokes you freely as you last-hit. Farm with Q Last Rites, soak her poke on ghouls from Shepherd of Souls, and don't chase her past the Tumble reset.","mid":"Levels 3-6 flatten into a skill window where your Mourning Mist mark and W cage can pin her Condemn, but the moment she hits Final Hour (R) at 6 she goes invisible on Tumble and kites your whole rotation. Play for prio and CS, keep W ready to wall her escape, and avoid open-ground fights.","late":"Vayne scales into a hypercarry that out-DPSes you if she itemizes; BotRK plus true damage shreds your HP and Condemn resets her every trade. Build armor, deny her with a split-push using Maiden and ghouls, and rely on your team to collapse on her squishy, immobile frame once her mobility is on cooldown.","whys":["Vayne's Tumble (Q) resets and true-damage Silver Bolts (W) win level 1.","At 2 her range and kiting keep her freely poking you down.","Level 3 evens as your Mourning Mist (E) mark and cage let you pin her.","Levels 4-5 stay even with W cage timing offsetting her Tumble spacing.","At 6 skill holds only if you dodge Final Hour (R) invisibility kiting.","First item swings back to Vayne as BotRK and true damage melt you.","Late, Vayne out-scales into a hypercarry that shreds your bruiser HP."]},
  {"a":"yorick","b":"vladimir","win":["Skill","Vladimir","Skill","Vladimir","Yorick","Vladimir","Vladimir"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 3-5","text":"Vladimir starts to out-sustain you: Transfusion (Q) heals him every trade and Sanguine Pool (W) dodges your Mourning Mist (E) mark and ghoul dashes entirely. Trade hard at level 1 before his Q is online; after that, poke and shove rather than commit."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"This is a Yorick window: Vladimir's Hemoplague (R) is a teamfight/burst tool, not a dueling out, so pre-6 you actually hold the club-you-down edge with ghouls and Maiden pressure. Use Eulogy of the Isles to force a shove and deny his free scaling farm."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Vladimir's item spike (Rylai's/Riftmaker) makes his Q poke and Pool sustain unbeatable in lane; you can't out-trade his healing anymore. Stop dueling, prioritize shoving with ghouls and roaming or taking plates instead."},{"when":"Late","text":"Vlad out-scales into an unkillable AP monster with Pool immunity and Hemoplague burst; your single-target split can't kill him and he heals through your ghouls. Group with your team, use Maiden to siege, and rely on grievous wounds to blunt his teamfight healing."}],"wants":{"you":["Level 1 all-in before Transfusion (Q) sustain is online","Level 5/6 ghoul-and-Maiden pressure to shove and deny farm","Grievous wounds to cut his Q and Hemoplague (R) healing"],"foe":["Transfusion (Q) sustain to heal through your trades","Sanguine Pool (W) to dodge your E mark, ghouls, and ganks","AP item scaling into an unkillable, high-burst late game"]},"early":"You actually win level 1: before Vladimir's Transfusion (Q) is leveled you out-damage him with Q Last Rites and ghoul autos, so all-in early. But by level 2 his Q sustain comes online and heals him through your trades, flipping the tempo to Vlad, so land your damage in that first-level window.","mid":"The mid-game seesaws: level 3 is even as you shove, level 4-5 Vlad's Sanguine Pool (W) starts dodging your Mourning Mist mark and ganks, but level 6 swings back to you because his Hemoplague (R) is a fight tool, not a duel-winner, and your ghoul-plus-Maiden pressure lets you shove and deny his farm. Hammer that pre-6 shove window.","late":"From his first item on, Vladimir's Q poke and Pool sustain become unbeatable in a duel and he scales into an unkillable AP threat with Hemoplague burst. Abandon the 1v1, group with Maiden to siege, buy grievous wounds to cut his healing, and let your team punish him since your split can't kill him alone.","whys":["Pre-Q he has no sustain, but 600-range poke keeps level 1 even.","At 2 Transfusion (Q) heals him through trades, flipping tempo to Vlad.","Level 3 evens out as you shove and he farms behind Q.","Levels 4-5 favour Vlad once Sanguine Pool (W) dodges your mark and ganks.","At 6 Yorick's ghoul-and-Maiden shove pressure beats his fight-only ult.","First item makes his Q/Pool sustain unbeatable in a duel, favouring Vlad.","Late, Vladimir out-scales into an unkillable AP burst threat."]},
  {"a":"yorick","b":"volibear","win":["Skill","Skill","Skill","Volibear","Volibear","Yorick","Yorick"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 3-5","text":"Volibear's spike: Thundering Smash (Q) speeds him up and stuns after chasing, and Frenzied Maul (W) heals and shreds you in melee. Don't let him ramp Q on you; use Mourning Mist (E) to slow his approach and hold W Dark Procession to cage him mid-chase."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Stormbringer (R) leaps 550 range on a 160/135/110s cooldown, slows everyone beneath him, grants him bonus health and disables your tower — that is the dive. Keep your HP topped, ward for his jungler, and hold Dark Procession to wall the landing so the dive stalls."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Yorick takes over: your ghoul swarm and Maiden out-DPS Volibear's bruiser sustain once you have items, and grievous wounds guts his Frenzied Maul healing. Shove him in with ghouls and force him to answer your push."},{"when":"Late","text":"Yorick wins the split cleanly: Maiden plus a full ghoul cage out-damages Voli in a sidelane and he can't leave without conceding your tower. His R is a great fight tool for his team, so don't let him roam free while you take his structures."}],"wants":{"you":["First item plus Maiden to out-DPS his bruiser sustain","Grievous wounds to cut Frenzied Maul (W) healing","Sidelane sims where ghouls swarm and Maiden shoves him in"],"foe":["Thundering Smash (Q) speed-and-stun to close and lock you","Frenzied Maul (W) healing and shred in melee brawls","Stormbringer (R) all-in and tower-dive with the untargetable leap"]},"early":"Levels 1-3 are a skill window: neither champ commits hard, but Volibear's Q speed lets him pick trades and his W heals if he lands autos. Farm with Q Last Rites, soak on ghouls from Shepherd of Souls, and use Mourning Mist (E) to slow his Thundering Smash approach so he can't ramp into a stun.","mid":"Levels 4-6 favour Volibear: his Q stun after chasing and Frenzied Maul sustain out-brawl you, and at 6 Stormbringer (R) leaps 550 range and disables your tower, so he can all-in or dive straight through your ghouls. Keep your HP topped, ping your jungler for dive threat, and don't stand in his kill range when his R is up.","late":"From your first item on, Yorick flips it: ghouls plus Maiden out-DPS Voli's sustain, grievous wounds neutralizes his Frenzied Maul healing, and your split-push forces him to respond. Cage him with W, swarm with ghouls, and make his lane presence a liability while your team leverages the map.","whys":["Level 1 is even; neither Volibear nor Yorick commits.","At 2 it stays skill as you farm and space his Q approach.","Level 3 remains even with careful kiting of his chase.","Levels 4-5 favour Voli once his Q stun and W sustain out-brawl you.","At 6 Stormbringer leaps 550 range and disables your tower for a dive.","First item plus Maiden lets your swarm out-DPS his bruiser sustain.","Late, Yorick's split and grievous wounds bury his single-target healing."]},
  {"a":"yorick","b":"warwick","win":["Warwick","Warwick","Skill","Skill","Yorick","Yorick","Yorick"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 3-5","text":"Warwick's early sustain is the problem: Jaws of the Beast (Q) heals him for the damage it deals, Blood Hunt (W) speeds him at you the moment you drop under 50%, and Primal Howl (E) cuts your burst for 2.5s. Trade in short bursts and use Mourning Mist (E) to slow the Blood Hunt chase."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Yorick's window opens: Infinite Duress (R) is a strong pick tool but is a fixed suppress you can pre-cage with W Dark Procession, and pre-Q-healing-items you now out-DPS him with ghouls and Maiden. Bait his E Primal Howl, then commit your combo behind a cage."},{"when":"1st item","text":"You're ahead here: your ghoul swarm plus Maiden out-damages Warwick's single-target sustain, and Bramble Vest's grievous wounds guts his Q and passive healing. Shove him in and deny his farm with constant push pressure."},{"when":"Late","text":"Yorick wins the sidelane outright: Maiden and a full ghoul cage out-DPS Warwick 1v1 and he can't leave your push without losing a tower. His R is a teamfight pick, so keep him lane-locked while your team plays the map 4v4."}],"wants":{"you":["Level 5+ ghoul-and-Maiden DPS to out-damage his sustain","Grievous wounds (Bramble) to cut Q and Blood Hunt healing","W Dark Procession cage to pre-empt his Infinite Duress (R) suppress"],"foe":["Jaws of the Beast (Q) sustain to heal through your early trades","Blood Hunt (W) speed to chase you under 50% HP","Primal Howl (E) to block your burst in extended brawls"]},"early":"Warwick wins levels 1-2: his Jaws of the Beast (Q) heals him through your trades, Blood Hunt (W) speeds him at you the moment you fall under 50% health, and his sustain out-lasts your early Q Last Rites pokes. Farm patiently, soak damage on ghouls from Shepherd of Souls, and don't dip under that 50% line while he holds W.","mid":"Level 3 evens as you shove and space, and by level 5-6 it swings to Yorick: pre-Q-healing-items you out-DPS Warwick with ghouls and Maiden, and his Infinite Duress (R) is a fixed suppress you can pre-cage with W Dark Procession. Bait his Primal Howl (E), then commit behind a cage and start denying his farm.","late":"From your first item on, Yorick controls the matchup: ghouls plus Maiden out-damage Warwick's single-target sustain, grievous wounds neutralizes his Q and passive healing, and your split-push keeps him lane-locked. Cage him, swarm him, and make his lack of waveclear a liability while your team plays 4v4.","whys":["Warwick's Jaws (Q) sustain heals through your level 1 trades.","At 2 his Blood Hunt chase and Q healing keep him ahead.","Level 3 evens out as you shove and space his engage.","Levels 4-5 stay even until your ghoul DPS starts to out-scale his sustain.","At 5/6 Yorick out-DPSes him with ghouls and can pre-cage his R.","First item plus Maiden and grievous wounds bury his single-target healing.","Late, Yorick's split and ghoul swarm win the sidelane outright."]},
  {"a":"yorick","b":"wukong","win":["Yorick","Skill","Skill","Wukong","Yorick","Yorick","Yorick"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 3-5","text":"Wukong's spike is level 4 when Warrior Trickster (W) plus Crushing Blow (Q) armour-shred lets him all-in: Nimbus Strike (E) in, Q to shred, then autos. Bait the clone with your Maiden and E the real body so your ghouls collapse — if he spends W to disengage without a kill, his escape is gone."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Cyclone (R) knocks up and spins, but if you've pre-placed W Dark Procession and have Maiden up, you tank the spin behind your cage while ghouls chunk him. Your ult swings 6 back your way — a wall of ghouls plus Maiden out-damages his combo if you don't get isolated."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Your Divine Sunderer/bramble spike stacks with Maiden's constant pressure; Wukong's item spike is Sundered Sky/Black Cleaver but a bruiser trade favours you once you have a wave of souls. Freeze and let ghouls grind — he can't crash safely."},{"when":"Late","text":"Split-push is your win con: Maiden plus ghouls shove towers no Wukong can 1v1, and his clone/Q burst does nothing to a wall of pets. Force him to answer your side lane and 4v5 your team."}],"wants":{"you":["Bait or E the clone so ghouls hit the real Wukong","Freeze near tower and win prolonged trades with Maiden","Pre-place W to wall Nimbus Strike and the R spin"],"foe":["Land Crushing Blow (Q) armour-shred, then all-in at 4-5","Use clone to dodge your E and reset a bad trade","Hit Cyclone (R) on an isolated Yorick away from ghouls"]},"early":"Levels 1-2 are yours — you out-trade with Q Last Rites healing and Wukong has no clone yet, so poke him whenever he steps for a minion. Respect his Q armour-shred but he can't commit hard this early.","mid":"Level 4 is his window: W clone plus Q shred enables an all-in, so play around your E slow and don't get caught without ghouls. Once you hit 6 with Maiden the lane swings back — pre-cage him and let souls grind him down.","late":"Post-Maiden and first item you dominate: constant ghoul pressure and split-push let you take towers Wukong can't defend. His burst is single-target and useless into your pet wall — make him respond to your split and win the map.","whys":["Level 1 favours you — Q Last Rites sustain out-trades Wukong before he has his clone.","Level 2 is even as Wukong gains a point but still lacks his all-in tools.","Level 3 stays skill-based; his combo isn't online and your poke matches his.","Level 4 is Wukong's spike — W clone plus Q armour-shred lets him all-in before your ghoul wall.","Level 6 swings to you — Maiden plus a pre-placed W cage lets you tank Cyclone and out-damage him.","First item favours you as Maiden's sustained pressure beats his bruiser burst.","Two-plus items are yours — split-push with ghouls and Maiden overpowers a single-target duelist."]},
  {"a":"yorick","b":"yasuo","win":["Yorick","Yorick","Yorick","Yorick","Yorick","Yasuo","Yasuo"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 3-5","text":"Yasuo can't Wind Wall (W) your ghouls or your Maiden's autos, so ghouls stroll through his shield and shred him. Wall down him with W Dark Procession when he dashes on a minion — trapped inside your cage with ghouls chewing, he has to burn Sweeping Blade (E) charges just to survive."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Last Breath (R) needs an airborne target and he makes his own: the third Steel Tempest fires a knock-up whirlwind at 475 range. Sidestep that cast and his 70/50/30s ult has nothing to blink to, while Maiden and the ghoul wall out-sustain his trades."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Yasuo's first crit item (IE/Shieldbow) is the swing — his output now passes your ghoul chip. Take Plated Steelcaps and Bramble, freeze the wave off him, and only take the fight while Wind Wall's 25/23/21/19/17s is still on cooldown."},{"when":"Late","text":"Late is Yasuo's window — with items and a teamfight around him he flanks and cleans up, and his ult finally comes online off your team's CC. Answer by split-pushing: your Maiden plus ghouls take towers he can't stop 1v1, so pressure the side and don't let him scale into a fight."}],"wants":{"you":["Cage him with W when he dashes so ghouls trap him","Keep E Mourning Mist slow on him to deny Sweeping Blade kiting","Freeze and win prolonged ghoul trades through his shield"],"foe":["Reach 2-item crit spike and CS evenly to scale","Find a knockup elsewhere to enable Last Breath (R)","Kite ghouls with E dashes and flank in teamfights"]},"early":"Levels 1-2 are firmly yours — Yasuo's Wind Wall does nothing to your ghouls or Maiden, and his flow shield gets bypassed by pet damage. Poke him with Q and E every time he goes for a minion.","mid":"Levels 3-6 stay dominant: cage him with W as he dashes, slow with E, and let ghouls grind through his shield. His R only lands off his own Q3 whirlwind, so sidestep that cast and the 1v1 stays yours.","late":"Two-plus items flip to Yasuo — full crit plus teamfight flanks let him carry, and his ult finally triggers off ally CC. Don't fight him into a scaled team; split-push instead, using Maiden and ghouls to take towers he can't defend alone.","whys":["Level 1 is yours — Wind Wall can't stop ghouls or Maiden and his shield is bypassed.","Level 2 stays yours as your Q and E poke chunk him with no counterplay.","Level 3 favours you — W cage plus ghouls trap him and force E charges.","Levels 4-5 remain yours with E slow denying his kiting through trades.","Level 6 is yours if you sidestep the Q3 whirlwind that feeds Last Breath.","First item still favours you as ghouls ignore his shield and freezes hold.","Two-plus items go to Yasuo — full crit and teamfight flanks finally out-scale you."]},
  {"a":"yorick","b":"yone","win":["Yone","Yone","Yone","Yone","Skill","Yone","Yone"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 3-5","text":"Yone's spike is brutal: the third Mortal Steel dashes him in with a knock-up, and Spirit Cleave (W) shields him on 14s through your ghoul chip. Soul Unbound (E) is not a dash — it snaps him back to the body he left behind, so cage that spot instead of chasing. Play behind minions and don't spend Maiden into his all-in."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Fate Sealed (R) blinks behind the last champion in a 1000-range line and drags everyone it hits toward him, on a 120/100/80s cooldown. Level 6 is roughly even: with Maiden up and a cage on his body you trade back, but a clean R still deletes you before ghouls stack. Respect the all-in unless you're clearly ahead."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Yone's item spike (IE/crit or Sundered Sky) plus E-reset safety makes him hard to punish; his shield eats your ghoul damage. Freeze if you can and farm — don't extend, because his mobility means you can't collapse on him the way you'd want."},{"when":"Late","text":"Yone out-duels and out-teamfights: E lets him dive and rewind out, R starts fights, and crit shreds you. Your only lever is the split — Maiden plus ghouls take towers he can't 1v1 fast, so pressure a side lane and avoid the straight duel."}],"wants":{"you":["Freeze and farm safely — deny his Q-in windows","Cage his body so the E snap-back lands in it","Split-push with Maiden to dodge his 1v1 dominance"],"foe":["Land Q third-hit knockup then W-shield the trade","Use E Soul Unbound to reset any bad all-in","Engage with Fate Sealed (R) before your ghouls stack"]},"early":"Levels 1-4 belong to Yone — his Q dash-knockup and W shield let him win every trade, and E Soul Unbound erases mistakes. Don't contest; concede a little CS, keep ghouls between you, and wait for your item and Maiden power.","mid":"Level 6 is a coin-flip: Fate Sealed can blow you up, but with Maiden and a well-timed W cage after his dash you can trade back. Only fight when you're ahead or he's out of E — otherwise farm and scale.","late":"Two-plus items keep favouring Yone in any duel or fight, thanks to crit, E safety, and R engage. Turn to your win con — split-push with ghouls and Maiden, take towers he can't defend alone, and force your team to punish his absence.","whys":["Level 1 favours Yone — his trading pattern and W shield beat your early ghoul chip.","Level 2 stays Yone's as Q ramps toward the knockup and you lack all-in tools.","Level 3 is Yone's spike with the Q knockup-dash online and E to reset.","Levels 4-5 remain his — mobility and shield deny you any clean cage.","Level 6 is even — Maiden plus a cage can answer Fate Sealed if you're not caught first.","First item favours Yone as crit plus E safety make him hard to punish.","Two-plus items stay Yone's — he out-duels and out-fights, leaving you only the split."]},
  {"a":"yorick","b":"zac","win":["Yorick","Skill","Skill","Yorick","Yorick","Yorick","Skill"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 3-5","text":"Zac's early trades lean on Stretching Strikes (Q), an 800-range grab on 14/12.5/11/9.5/8s, plus the Elastic Slingshot engage — but he is low-damage and blob-reliant. Level 4 is your spike: cage him with W as he lands his E, slow with Mourning Mist, and ghouls plus Maiden out-DPS him. Walk over every blob to deny the heal."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Let's Bounce! (R) knocks up and slows on a 120/105/90s cooldown, but it is a teamfight tool rather than a duel button. This is your window — with Maiden up and ghouls stacked you shove and out-sustain him; Zac farms and waits for objectives. Zone him off the wave with the cage."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Your first item plus Maiden is a hard spike here — Zac scales into a tank/engage role and can't answer sustained ghoul pressure. Freeze or shove and threaten his tower; his blob-heal can't keep up with a full Maiden and soul wall."},{"when":"Late","text":"Late is skill/even — Zac's value is roaming and R engaging fights, not the side lane, so he'll leave to impact the map. Match him by split-pushing: your ghouls and Maiden take towers, but respect his global E/R roam threat and ward so you don't get collapsed on."}],"wants":{"you":["Cage him with W as he lands Slingshot (E) engage","Step on his passive blobs to deny the sustain","Shove with Maiden while his R is useless in a 1v1"],"foe":["Unstable Matter chip while his Q holds you","Roam and impact other lanes rather than duel","Save Let's Bounce (R) for a teamfight engage"]},"early":"Level 1-2 favour you — Zac is low-damage early and you out-trade with Q sustain and E poke. Watch his Q pull but punish him every time he steps up for a minion.","mid":"Levels 4-6 are firmly yours: cage his E engage, slow him, and let Maiden plus ghouls grind him down. His R is a fight tool that does nothing to you 1v1, so shove hard and deny his farm while stepping on his heal blobs.","late":"Two-plus items even out — Zac's job is roaming and R-engaging fights, not winning the side lane. Take the split with ghouls and Maiden, but ward for his long-range E roam so his engage doesn't catch you out.","whys":["Level 1 favours you — you out-trade a low-damage early Zac with Q sustain.","Level 2 is even as Zac gains his Q pull and blob sustain to stabilise.","Level 3 stays skill-based; neither has a clean all-in yet.","Level 4 is yours — W cage on his E engage plus Maiden out-DPS him.","Level 6 favours you because his R is a fight tool, useless in a lane 1v1.","First item is yours as Maiden's sustained pressure beats his blob heal.","Two-plus items even out — Zac shifts to roaming and teamfight engage."]},
  {"a":"yorick","b":"ziggs","win":["Ziggs","Ziggs","Skill","Ziggs","Skill","Ziggs","Ziggs"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 3-5","text":"Ziggs pokes you off the wave with Bouncing Bomb (Q), 850 range on 6/5.5/5/4.5/4s, and zones your minions and ghouls with Hexplosive Minefield (E) on a flat 16s; every walk-up costs you health. Satchel Charge (W) then knocks you away on 20/18/16/14/12s to break the all-in. Farm behind ghouls and don't get poked to death."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Mega Inferno Bomb (R) adds waveclear and long-range execute pressure. This stays his — he shoves you in and pokes over the wall while you're stuck under tower. Use Maiden to help hold the wave and soak poke, but you won't kill a Ziggs who plays back behind his mines."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Ziggs' first item (Liandry's/Luden's) ramps his poke and waveclear hard; he out-ranges everything you have and his W plus Satchel deny your engage. Freeze is nearly impossible against his shove. Look to roam or wait for jungle ganks — his Satchel and mines make solo dives painful."},{"when":"Late","text":"Late is a race: Ziggs out-pokes and out-clears in lane, but he's immobile and squishy, and your Maiden plus ghouls take towers faster than he can defend. This is your only edge — split-push relentlessly, avoid the poke war, and force him to answer a side lane where his poke doesn't stop a soul wave."}],"wants":{"you":["Use ghouls to soak Q poke and farm at range","Roam or set up ganks — Satchel makes solo dives hard","Split-push with Maiden to out-tower his immobility"],"foe":["Zone the wave with E mines and chunk you with Q","Knock you back with Satchel Charge (W) to deny all-ins","Shove you under tower and poke over the wall"]},"early":"Levels 1-2 are Ziggs' — his 850-range Q out-ranges you and his E mines zone your approach and your ghouls. Don't trade into the poke; last-hit carefully with ghoul help and accept that you'll take chip.","mid":"Levels 3-6 stay his: he shoves you in, pokes over the wall, and Satchel Charge knocks you away whenever you commit. Use Maiden to hold the wave and reduce poke, but you can't kill a Ziggs who respects his mines — look to roam or set up jungle pressure instead.","late":"Two-plus items keep the poke war in Ziggs' favour, but he's immobile and can't defend towers. Turn to the split — Maiden plus ghouls crash and kill turrets faster than he clears, so drag him around the map instead of dueling into his range.","whys":["Level 1 favours Ziggs — his Q out-ranges you and mines zone your walk-up.","Level 2 stays his as W plus Q chunk you off every last-hit attempt.","Level 3 is even — with ghouls and E you can farm through the poke.","Levels 4-5 favour Ziggs; Satchel denies your all-in while he shoves and pokes.","Level 6 is even — Maiden helps hold the wave and soak his R and poke.","First item is Ziggs' as Liandry's/Luden's ramps poke and waveclear you can't match.","Two-plus items stay his in the poke war, leaving you only the split to punish his immobility."]}
